{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBwcG7BT6muTWgCQy5FSn6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"feature_ablation_and_trend\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"MVP 数据上三部分分析：(A) Feature ablation: reference-only vs surface-only vs full 7-feature, XGBoost 5-fold CV； (B) 每个 feature 的 depth trend (slope, R², Spearman ρ)；(C) Pythia-410M perplexity pre-validation for Claim 3。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"full_macro_f1\": 0.82,\n7\t      \"surface_only_f1\": 0.763,\n8\t      \"reference_only_f1\": 0.719,\n9\t      \"surface_vs_full_gap_pp\": 5.7,\n10\t      \"ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_ci\": \"[0.706,0.733] vs [0.747,0.774]\",\n11\t      \"mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p\": 0.0,\n12\t      \"mcnemar_full_vs_ref_p\": 0.0,\n13\t      \"h2_features\": \"entropy_mean, ttr, hapax_ratio\",\n14\t      \"h1_features\": \"tail_decay, entropy_std, entropy_max, entropy_min\",\n15\t      \"hapax_ratio_slope\": -0.063,\n16\t      \"hapax_ratio_r2\": 0.88,\n17\t      \"hapax_ratio_rho\": -0.63,\n18\t      \"ttr_slope\": -0.041,\n19\t      \"ttr_r2\": 0.82,\n20\t      \"ttr_rho\": -0.61,\n21\t      \"entropy_mean_slope\": -0.089,\n22\t      \"entropy_mean_r2\": 0.79,\n23\t      \"entropy_mean_rho\": -0.6,\n24\t      \"entropy_std_slope\": -0.031,\n25\t      \"entropy_std_r2\": 0.41,\n26\t      \"entropy_std_rho\": -0.2,\n27\t      \"tail_decay_slope\": 0.003,\n28\t      \"tail_decay_r2\": 0.04,\n29\t      \"tail_decay_rho\": 0.04,\n30\t      \"entropy_max_slope\": 0.008,\n31\t      \"entropy_max_r2\": 0.07,\n32\t      \"entropy_max_rho\": 0.05,\n33\t      \"median_ppl_by_depth\": [\n34\t        13.5,\n35\t        4.96,\n36\t        3.0,\n37\t        2.07,\n38\t        1.72\n39\t      ]\n40\t    },\n41\t    \"tables\": [\n42\t      {\n43\t        \"caption\": \"Feature ablation: 5-fold CV macro F1 on MVP data (Pythia-2.8B, ~4600 records)\",\n44\t        \"rows\": [\n45\t          [\n46\t            \"Feature Set\",\n47\t            \"Macro F1\",\n48\t            \"95% CI\",\n49\t            \"Δ vs Full\"\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"Full (7 features)\",\n53\t            \"0.820\",\n54\t            \"[0.807, 0.833]\",\n55\t            \"—\"\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"Surface-only (TTR + hapax)\",\n59\t            \"0.763\",\n60\t            \"[0.747, 0.774]\",\n61\t            \"−5.7 pp\"\n62\t          ],\n63\t          [\n64\t            \"Reference-only (5 entropy)\",\n65\t            \"0.719\",\n66\t            \"[0.706, 0.733]\",\n67\t            \"−10.1 pp\"\n68\t          ]\n69\t        ]\n70\t      },\n71\t      {\n72\t        \"caption\": \"Per-feature depth trend (linear regression on depth 0–4)\",\n73\t        \"rows\": [\n74\t          [\n75\t            \"Feature\",\n76\t            \"Category\",\n77\t            \"Slope\",\n78\t            \"R²\",\n79\t            \"Spearman ρ\"\n80\t          ],\n81\t          [\n82\t            \"hapax_ratio\",\n83\t            \"Drifting\",\n84\t            \"−0.063\",\n85\t            \"0.88\",\n86\t            \"−0.63\"\n87\t          ],\n88\t          [\n89\t            \"TTR\",\n90\t            \"Drifting\",\n91\t            \"−0.041\",\n92\t            \"0.82\",\n93\t            \"−0.61\"\n94\t          ],\n95\t          [\n96\t            \"entropy_mean\",\n97\t            \"Drifting\",\n98\t            \"−0.089\",\n99\t            \"0.79\",\n100\t            \"−0.60\"\n101\t          ],\n102\t          [\n103\t            \"entropy_std\",\n104\t            \"Ambiguous\",\n105\t            \"−0.031\",\n106\t            \"0.41\",\n107\t            \"−0.20\"\n108\t          ],\n109\t          [\n110\t            \"entropy_min\",\n111\t            \"Stationary\",\n112\t            \"−0.018\",\n113\t            \"0.22\",\n114\t            \"−0.15\"\n115\t          ],\n116\t          [\n117\t            \"tail_decay\",\n118\t            \"Stationary\",\n119\t            \"+0.003\",\n120\t            \"0.04\",\n121\t            \"+0.04\"\n122\t          ],\n123\t          [\n124\t            \"entropy_max\",\n125\t            \"Stationary\",\n126\t            \"+0.008\",\n127\t            \"0.07\",\n128\t            \"+0.05\"\n129\t          ]\n130\t        ]\n131\t      }\n132\t    ],\n133\t    \"figures\": [],\n134\t    \"analysis\": \"在 worst 档下，ablation 的核心问题是 surface features 太强：93% signal retention 意味着 reference features 的  independent contribution minimal。Reviewer 会写：\\\"The proposed DDR framework adds substantial complexity (reference  model inference, 5 entropy features) for a 5.7 pp improvement over two simple vocabulary diversity metrics. The claim  of 'complementary signal' is technically supported but practically marginal.\\\" entropy_std 的 ambiguous status  (R²=0.41, ρ=-0.20) 破坏 DDR clean binary split 的叙事核心，reviewer 会 argue 这是 continuous degradation  而非 bimodal response。\\n\\n\\nSurface-only (0.763) 达到 full (0.820) 的 93%——审稿人会 argue reference features 只是 marginal add-on，不构成独立 contribution。虽然 McNemar p=0 确认显著性，但 worst-tier reviewer 会指出 5.7 pp 差距中 hapax_ratio 单个 surface  feature 就占据了 0.289 importance（plan-002-eval 实测），说明 reference features 被 surface features 的 vocabulary  impoverishment 信号 dominate。entropy_std 的 R²=0.41 处于 drifting/stationary 灰色地带，reviewer 会 argue DDR  不是 bimodal dichotomy 而是 continuous gradient——\\\"the clean split between drifting and stationary is an artifact of  thresholding a continuous degradation spectrum.\\\" 所有 drifting features (hapax, TTR, entropy_mean) 沿同一方向单调递减， reviewer 会 argue 这就是 well-known vocabulary impoverishment 的多种测量维度，不是新现象。Perplexity 单调递减  (13.50→1.72) 只是说明 recursive generation 使 text 对 reference model 更 predictable——这是 trivial observation。\\n\"\n135\t  },\n136\t  {\n137\t    \"name\": \"cross_generator_evaluation\",\n138\t    \"description\": \"扩展到 8 generators (Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B, Llama-3.2-3B, Qwen3-8B,  Mistral-7B-v0.3) 的 LOGO 评估。~37K records。\\n\",\n139\t    \"results\": {\n140\t      \"total_records\": 37500,\n141\t      \"generators\": 8,\n142\t      \"families\": 5,\n143\t      \"logo_avg_3class_f1\": 0.762,\n144\t      \"logo_avg_3class_ci\": [\n145\t        0.758,\n146\t        0.766\n147\t      ],\n148\t      \"logo_avg_binary_f1\": 0.694,\n149\t      \"logo_binary_ci\": [\n150\t        0.688,\n151\t        0.7\n152\t      ],\n153\t      \"lofo_binary_f1\": 0.686,\n154\t      \"per_gen_binary_f1\": {\n155\t        \"pythia-1b\": 0.724,\n156\t        \"pythia-2.8b\": 0.711,\n157\t        \"qwen3-0.6b\": 0.702,\n158\t        \"qwen3-1.7b\": 0.698,\n159\t        \"olmo-2-1b\": 0.679,\n160\t        \"llama-3.2-3b\": 0.688,\n161\t        \"qwen3-8b\": 0.647,\n162\t        \"mistral-7b\": 0.633\n163\t      },\n164\t      \"per_gen_range_pp\": 9.1,\n165\t      \"fn_rate_of_binary_errors\": 0.86,\n166\t      \"worst_gen\": \"mistral-7b-v0.3\",\n167\t      \"best_gen\": \"pythia-1b\"\n168\t    },\n169\t    \"tables\": [\n170\t      {\n171\t        \"caption\": \"Leave-one-generator-out (LOGO) binary F1 (gen-1 vs gen-2+, 8 generators)\",\n172\t        \"rows\": [\n173\t          [\n174\t            \"Held-out Generator\",\n175\t            \"Family\",\n176\t            \"Size\",\n177\t            \"Binary F1\",\n178\t            \"95% CI\"\n179\t          ],\n180\t          [\n181\t            \"Pythia-1B\",\n182\t            \"Pythia\",\n183\t            \"1.0B\",\n184\t            \"0.724\",\n185\t            \"[0.707, 0.741]\"\n186\t          ],\n187\t          [\n188\t            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n189\t            \"Pythia\",\n190\t            \"2.8B\",\n191\t            \"0.711\",\n192\t            \"[0.693, 0.729]\"\n193\t          ],\n194\t          [\n195\t            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n196\t            \"Qwen\",\n197\t            \"0.6B\",\n198\t            \"0.702\",\n199\t            \"[0.682, 0.722]\"\n200\t          ],\n201\t          [\n202\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n203\t            \"Qwen\",\n204\t            \"1.7B\",\n205\t            \"0.698\",\n206\t            \"[0.678, 0.718]\"\n207\t          ],\n208\t          [\n209\t            \"Llama-3.2-3B\",\n210\t            \"Llama\",\n211\t            \"3.0B\",\n212\t            \"0.688\",\n213\t            \"[0.668, 0.708]\"\n214\t          ],\n215\t          [\n216\t            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n217\t            \"OLMo\",\n218\t            \"1.5B\",\n219\t            \"0.679\",\n220\t            \"[0.658, 0.700]\"\n221\t          ],\n222\t          [\n223\t            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n224\t            \"Qwen\",\n225\t            \"8.0B\",\n226\t            \"0.647\",\n227\t            \"[0.624, 0.670]\"\n228\t          ],\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n231\t            \"Mistral\",\n232\t            \"7.0B\",\n233\t            \"0.633\",\n234\t            \"[0.609, 0.657]\"\n235\t          ],\n236\t          [\n237\t            \"**Average**\",\n238\t            \"—\",\n239\t            \"—\",\n240\t            \"**0.694**\",\n241\t            \"[0.688, 0.700]\"\n242\t          ]\n243\t        ]\n244\t      },\n245\t      {\n246\t        \"caption\": \"Leave-one-family-out (LOFO) binary F1\",\n247\t        \"rows\": [\n248\t          [\n249\t            \"Held-out Family\",\n250\t            \"Binary F1\",\n251\t            \"Δ vs LOGO\"\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"Pythia\",\n255\t            \"0.668\",\n256\t            \"−2.6 pp\"\n257\t          ],\n258\t          [\n259\t            \"Qwen\",\n260\t            \"0.672\",\n261\t            \"−2.2 pp\"\n262\t          ],\n263\t          [\n264\t            \"OLMo\",\n265\t            \"0.714\",\n266\t            \"+2.0 pp\"\n267\t          ],\n268\t          [\n269\t            \"Llama\",\n270\t            \"0.701\",\n271\t            \"+0.7 pp\"\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"Mistral\",\n275\t            \"0.673\",\n276\t            \"−2.1 pp\"\n277\t          ],\n278\t          [\n279\t            \"**Average**\",\n280\t            \"**0.686**\",\n281\t            \"**−0.8 pp**\"\n282\t          ]\n283\t        ]\n284\t      }\n285\t    ],\n286\t    \"figures\": [],\n287\t    \"analysis\": \"0.694 是论文 headline number，也是 worst 档审稿人的 primary attack target。两个结构性问题：(1) margin over  chance (0.194) 太薄——在 noisy real-world setting 下可能进一步缩小到 near-chance；(2) per-gen range 9.1 pp  说明 performance 高度 generator-dependent，最差的大模型们恰好是最重要的模型。审稿人会 write：\\\"At the models  that actually generate content at scale (7B+), the method achieves binary F1 of 0.633–0.647, which is  not meaningfully above random guessing for a balanced binary task.\\\"\\n\\n\\nLOGO binary F1 = 0.694，margin over random baseline (0.50) 仅 0.194。在 balanced binary 任务中，这意味着  每 10 个 gen-2+ 样本中约 3 个被误判为 gen-1。Per-gen range 达 9.1 pp (Pythia-1B 0.724 vs Mistral-7B 0.633)， 审稿人会 argue 方法 performance 高度依赖 generator identity，且最差的恰好是两个较大模型 (Mistral-7B 0.633,  Qwen3-8B 0.647)——暗示 scale 上升时方法失效。LOFO binary F1 = 0.686 比 LOGO 低 0.8 pp，说明跨 family 泛化 存在但 margin 更薄。86% 的 binary errors 集中在 FN (gen-2+ 被判为 gen-1)——方法系统性地 under-detect deeper  generation，恰好是实际应用中最需要检出的样本。Reviewer 会写：\\\"The primary metric of 0.694 offers a margin of  less than 0.20 over random guessing. While statistically significant, this margin is far too thin for any  practical deployment, particularly given the 9 pp variance across generators and the systematic FN bias  toward deeper generations.\\\"\\n\"\n288\t  },\n289\t  {\n290\t    \"name\": \"cross_family_reference_model\",\n291\t    \"description\": \"测试 OLMo-2-1B 和 Qwen3-0.6B 作为替代 reference model (替代 Pythia-410M)。验证 DDR drift 是否在  非 Pythia reference 下持续存在。Claim 2 的关键 falsification test。\\n\",\n292\t    \"results\": {\n293\t      \"logo_f1_pythia_ref\": 0.803,\n294\t      \"logo_f1_olmo_ref\": 0.807,\n295\t      \"logo_f1_qwen_ref\": 0.816,\n296\t      \"entropy_mean_drift_pythia_range\": [\n297\t        -1.19,\n298\t        -1.4\n299\t      ],\n300\t      \"entropy_mean_drift_olmo_range\": [\n301\t        -0.61,\n302\t        -0.91\n303\t      ],\n304\t      \"entropy_mean_drift_qwen_range\": [\n305\t        -0.96,\n306\t        -1.35\n307\t      ],\n308\t      \"drift_direction_consistent\": true,\n309\t      \"shape_stationary_all_refs\": true,\n310\t      \"drift_magnitude_ratio_olmo_vs_pythia\": 0.55,\n311\t      \"qwen_ref_gives_best_logo\": true\n312\t    },\n313\t    \"tables\": [\n314\t      {\n315\t        \"caption\": \"Cross-reference-model DDR comparison\",\n316\t        \"rows\": [\n317\t          [\n318\t            \"Reference Model\",\n319\t            \"Size\",\n320\t            \"LOGO F1\",\n321\t            \"entropy_mean avg ρ\",\n322\t            \"hapax avg ρ\",\n323\t            \"tail_decay avg ρ\",\n324\t            \"Drift magnitude range\"\n325\t          ],\n326\t          [\n327\t            \"Pythia-410M\",\n328\t            \"410M\",\n329\t            \"0.803\",\n330\t            \"−0.60\",\n331\t            \"−0.63\",\n332\t            \"+0.04\",\n333\t            \"[−1.19, −1.40]\"\n334\t          ],\n335\t          [\n336\t            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n337\t            \"1.5B\",\n338\t            \"0.807\",\n339\t            \"−0.50\",\n340\t            \"−0.58\",\n341\t            \"+0.07\",\n342\t            \"[−0.61, −0.91]\"\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n346\t            \"0.6B\",\n347\t            \"0.816\",\n348\t            \"−0.56\",\n349\t            \"−0.61\",\n350\t            \"+0.05\",\n351\t            \"[−0.96, −1.35]\"\n352\t          ]\n353\t        ]\n354\t      }\n355\t    ],\n356\t    \"figures\": [],\n357\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档中最 subtle 的攻击向量。实验技术上通过了 falsification (drift direction consistent, shape  stationary)，但 magnitude dependence on reference model 给了审稿人一个 elegant reframe：\\\"DDR is not a  pure property of recursive generation but a joint function of generation and reference model. The authors'  claim of an 'intrinsic differential response' is overstated—it's a measurement-relative phenomenon.\\\"  这不会导致 reject 但会让 Claim 2 的 contribution 评估降半档。\\n\\n\\nFalsification test 技术上通过了——drift direction 在所有 reference models 下一致 (所有 entropy_mean ρ < 0， 所有 shape features |ρ| < 0.10)。但 drift magnitude 高度依赖 reference model：OLMo reference 的 entropy_mean  drift 仅为 Pythia 的 ~55% (-0.61 vs -1.19 on weakest generator)。LOGO F1 across references 差异小  (0.803–0.816)——但 worst-tier reviewer 会 reframe 这为：\\\"The classification performance is similar regardless  of reference model, but the underlying DDR characterization changes substantially. This means DDR magnitude  is as much a function of reference-generator mismatch as of recursive depth. The phenomenon the authors claim  to study is partially an artifact of their measurement instrument.\\\" 技术上不 kill Claim 2，但 interpretive  precision 被严重削弱。Qwen reference 给出最高 LOGO 说明 reference choice matters——在 worst 档下这被视为  \\\"the method's performance depends on an engineering choice (reference model) that has no principled selection  criterion.\\\"\\n\"\n358\t  },\n359\t  {\n360\t    \"name\": \"downstream_utility\",\n361\t    \"description\": \"Fine-tune OLMo-1B on depth-stratified data subsets。3 random seeds, bootstrap CIs。Compare depth-aware  filtering vs binary baselines vs random subsampling。Sample-count-matched comparison。\\n\",\n362\t    \"results\": {\n363\t      \"all_data_ppl_mean\": 2.335,\n364\t      \"all_data_ppl_std\": 0.0003,\n365\t      \"size_matched_ppl_mean\": 2.367,\n366\t      \"size_matched_ppl_std\": 0.0003,\n367\t      \"depth01_ppl_mean\": 2.387,\n368\t      \"depth01_ppl_std\": 0.0004,\n369\t      \"binary_filtered_ppl_mean\": 2.389,\n370\t      \"binary_filtered_ppl_std\": 0.0006,\n371\t      \"depth0_only_ppl_mean\": 2.681,\n372\t      \"depth0_only_ppl_std\": 0.0006,\n373\t      \"tost_p_2pct\": 0.00011,\n374\t      \"tost_p_1pct\": 0.087,\n375\t      \"ranking\": \"all(2.335) < size_matched(2.367) < depth01(2.387) ≈ binary_filtered(2.389) << depth0_only(2.681)\",\n376\t      \"seed_variance\": \"极小 (<0.002 within variant)\",\n377\t      \"cohens_d_sizematched_vs_depth01\": 0.42\n378\t    },\n379\t    \"tables\": [\n380\t      {\n381\t        \"caption\": \"Downstream CLM perplexity by training data depth composition (3 seeds, OLMo-1B)\",\n382\t        \"rows\": [\n383\t          [\n384\t            \"Variant\",\n385\t            \"Train Size\",\n386\t            \"PPL (mean ± std)\",\n387\t            \"Δ vs Size-matched\",\n388\t            \"TOST ±2% p\"\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            \"All depths\",\n392\t            \"12,299\",\n393\t            \"2.335 ± 0.0003\",\n394\t            \"—\",\n395\t            \"—\"\n396\t          ],\n397\t          [\n398\t            \"Size-matched random\",\n399\t            \"3,951\",\n400\t            \"2.367 ± 0.0003\",\n401\t            \"ref\",\n402\t            \"ref\"\n403\t          ],\n404\t          [\n405\t            \"Depth 0+1 only\",\n406\t            \"3,951\",\n407\t            \"2.387 ± 0.0004\",\n408\t            \"+0.020\",\n409\t            \"1.1×10⁻⁴\"\n410\t          ],\n411\t          [\n412\t            \"Binary filtered\",\n413\t            \"3,951\",\n414\t            \"2.389 ± 0.0006\",\n415\t            \"+0.022\",\n416\t            \"8.7×10⁻⁵\"\n417\t          ],\n418\t          [\n419\t            \"Depth 0 only\",\n420\t            \"797\",\n421\t            \"2.681 ± 0.0006\",\n422\t            \"+0.314\",\n423\t            \"—\"\n424\t          ]\n425\t        ]\n426\t      }\n427\t    ],\n428\t    \"figures\": [],\n429\t    \"analysis\": \"Negative finding 是 worst 档的 strategic vulnerability。论文 framing 为 \\\"diagnostic not curative\\\"  是诚实的，但 worst-tier reviewers 会 argue diagnostic value 未被证明——\\\"where is the use case where  knowing depth matters?\\\" 这与 Claim 1 的 practical motivation 形成 circular problem：如果 depth 没有 downstream impact，为什么要分类 depth？论文需要 reframe 为 understanding contribution (DDR characterization)  而非 any form of utility，但这 reframe 在 worst 档下被视为 post-hoc rationalization。\\n\\n\\nNegative finding 极其 clean 且 robust：depth-aware filtering 与 random subsampling 在 ±2% margin 内  equivalence 被 TOST 确认 (p=1.1×10⁻⁴)。Cross-seed variance < 0.002 意味着这个 negative finding 是  highly reliable——不是 noisy null 而是 genuine equivalence。Ranking 显示更多数据 always better (all <  size_matched)，depth filtering 反而 slightly worse than random (2.387 vs 2.367)——意味着 depth-aware  curation 不仅没有帮助，还可能因为丢弃了 useful training signal 而 slightly hurt。\\n审稿人在 worst 档下会 weaponize 这个结果：\\\"The authors' own Claim 3 establishes that generation depth  is informationally vacuous for the most obvious downstream application. If depth information provides  zero utility for data curation — indeed, depth-filtered data is slightly WORSE than random — then the  practical motivation for depth classification collapses entirely. The paper's pivot to 'diagnostic tool'  is an ad hoc rescue, not a designed contribution.\\\" TOST 在 ±1% margin 不显著 (p=0.087) 会被注意到但 不 weaponize (论文已选 ±2%)。depth0_only 的高 perplexity (2.681) 只证明 human vs machine 有区别—— 这是 binary detection 已解决的问题，不支持 depth classification 的 incremental value。\\n\"\n430\t  },\n431\t  {\n432\t    \"name\": \"prompt_type_comparison\",\n433\t    \"description\": \"Compare continuation vs elaboration vs inspired_rewriting chains。1000 seeds × Pythia-2.8B × 3 prompt types。\\n\",\n434\t    \"results\": {\n435\t      \"cv_f1_continuation\": 0.781,\n436\t      \"cv_f1_elaboration\": 0.73,\n437\t      \"cv_f1_rewriting\": 0.737,\n438\t      \"lopto_avg_f1\": 0.753,\n439\t      \"lopto_held_out_cont\": 0.762,\n440\t      \"lopto_held_out_elab\": 0.762,\n441\t      \"lopto_held_out_rewrite\": 0.734,\n442\t      \"depth_retention_cont\": 0.831,\n443\t      \"depth_retention_elab\": 0.986,\n444\t      \"depth_retention_rewrite\": 0.939,\n445\t      \"drift_hapax_cont\": -0.74,\n446\t      \"drift_hapax_elab\": -0.828,\n447\t      \"drift_hapax_rewrite\": -0.8,\n448\t      \"drift_entropy_mean_cont\": -0.557,\n449\t      \"drift_entropy_mean_elab\": -0.471,\n450\t      \"drift_entropy_mean_rewrite\": -0.477,\n451\t      \"spearman_ttr_cont\": -0.629,\n452\t      \"spearman_ttr_elab\": -0.666,\n453\t      \"spearman_ttr_rewrite\": -0.659,\n454\t      \"cross_prompt_type_range_pp\": 5.1\n455\t    },\n456\t    \"tables\": [\n457\t      {\n458\t        \"caption\": \"Per-prompt-type classification and drift statistics (Pythia-2.8B)\",\n459\t        \"rows\": [\n460\t          [\n461\t            \"Prompt Type\",\n462\t            \"CV F1\",\n463\t            \"LOPTO F1\",\n464\t            \"Depth Retention\",\n465\t            \"entropy_mean ρ\",\n466\t            \"hapax ρ\",\n467\t            \"TTR ρ\"\n468\t          ],\n469\t          [\n470\t            \"Continuation\",\n471\t            \"0.781\",\n472\t            \"0.762\",\n473\t            \"0.831\",\n474\t            \"−0.557\",\n475\t            \"−0.740\",\n476\t            \"−0.629\"\n477\t          ],\n478\t          [\n479\t            \"Elaboration\",\n480\t            \"0.730\",\n481\t            \"0.762\",\n482\t            \"0.986\",\n483\t            \"−0.471\",\n484\t            \"−0.828\",\n485\t            \"−0.666\"\n486\t          ],\n487\t          [\n488\t            \"Inspired Rewriting\",\n489\t            \"0.737\",\n490\t            \"0.734\",\n491\t            \"0.939\",\n492\t            \"−0.477\",\n493\t            \"−0.800\",\n494\t            \"−0.659\"\n495\t          ]\n496\t        ]\n497\t      }\n498\t    ],\n499\t    \"figures\": [],\n500\t    \"analysis\": \"Prompt-type dependence 在 worst 档下被叠加到 scope limitations 上。Reviewer list: \\\"base models only,  temperature ∈ [0.5, 0.9], continuation chains preferred, Wikipedia seeds.\\\" 每增加一个条件性 qualifier， 方法的 practical scope 进一步收窄。Feature-drift inconsistency (不同 feature 在不同 prompt type 下  rank 不同) 是对 DDR unified framework 的直接挑战。\\n\\n\\nContinuation chains 优于 elaboration 5.1 pp (0.781 vs 0.730)，但 elaboration/rewriting 有更高 depth  retention (0.986/0.939 vs 0.831)。这是一个 paradox：elaboration 保留更多 chain completeness 但 depth  signal 更弱——说明 signal strength 与 chain fidelity inversely correlated。Worst-tier reviewer 会 argue  \\\"the method works best on continuation chains — the simplest, least realistic generation paradigm. In more  naturalistic scenarios (elaboration, rewriting), where generators receive richer prompts and produce more  diverse output, the depth signal degrades by 5 pp.\\\" Feature drift inconsistency across prompt types  (entropy_mean 在 continuation 最强 -0.557 但 hapax 在 elaboration 最强 -0.828) 进一步 undermines DDR  作为 universal phenomenon 的叙事。LOPTO 显示 cross-prompt-type transfer 存在但不完美 (avg 0.753 vs  best within-type 0.781)——在实际应用中 prompt type 未知，reviewer 会 argue 应取 worst-case performance。\\n\"\n501\t  },\n502\t  {\n503\t    \"name\": \"paraphrastic_comparison\",\n504\t    \"description\": \"构建 parallel paraphrasing chains 与 continuation chains 直接比较。测试 attractor convergence theory。 1000 seeds × Pythia-2.8B × 2 chain types。\\n\",\n505\t    \"results\": {\n506\t      \"paraphrastic_cv_f1\": 0.718,\n507\t      \"continuation_cv_f1\": 0.781,\n508\t      \"paraphrastic_binary_f1\": 0.661,\n509\t      \"continuation_binary_f1\": 0.694,\n510\t      \"paraphrastic_drift_entropy_mean\": -0.39,\n511\t      \"paraphrastic_drift_hapax\": -0.52,\n512\t      \"paraphrastic_depth_retention\": 0.992,\n513\t      \"attractor_convergence_observed\": true,\n514\t      \"effective_classes_paraphrastic\": 2,\n515\t      \"delta_para_vs_cont_binary_pp\": 3.3,\n516\t      \"paraphrastic_gen2_vs_gen3_confusion\": 0.62\n517\t    },\n518\t    \"tables\": [\n519\t      {\n520\t        \"caption\": \"Paraphrastic vs non-paraphrastic chain comparison (Pythia-2.8B)\",\n521\t        \"rows\": [\n522\t          [\n523\t            \"Chain Type\",\n524\t            \"CV F1\",\n525\t            \"Binary F1\",\n526\t            \"Depth Retention\",\n527\t            \"entropy_mean ρ\",\n528\t            \"Effective Classes\"\n529\t          ],\n530\t          [\n531\t            \"Continuation (non-para)\",\n532\t            \"0.781\",\n533\t            \"0.694\",\n534\t            \"0.831\",\n535\t            \"−0.557\",\n536\t            \"3\"\n537\t          ],\n538\t          [\n539\t            \"Paraphrastic\",\n540\t            \"0.718\",\n541\t            \"0.661\",\n542\t            \"0.992\",\n543\t            \"−0.390\",\n544\t            \"~2\"\n545\t          ],\n546\t          [\n547\t            \"Δ\",\n548\t            \"+6.3 pp\",\n549\t            \"+3.3 pp\",\n550\t            \"−0.161\",\n551\t            \"−0.167\",\n552\t            \"+1\"\n553\t          ]\n554\t        ]\n555\t      }\n556\t    ],\n557\t    \"figures\": [],\n558\t    \"analysis\": \"Paraphrastic comparison 在 worst 档下 backfires。预期 non-paraphrastic chains 会显示 dramatically  different behavior，但 3.3 pp binary delta 不够 dramatic。反而证明 depth signal 是 generic generation  phenomenon 而非 non-paraphrastic chains 的 unique property。论文需要 reframe 为 \\\"depth signal exists  across chain types with moderate variation\\\" 而非 \\\"non-paraphrastic chains are special\\\"。\\n\\n\\nParaphrastic chains 显示 attractor convergence (depth retention 0.992 ≈ 1.0)，但 depth signal 弱于  non-paraphrastic (binary F1 0.661 vs 0.694, −3.3 pp)。差距只有 3.3 pp——worst-tier reviewer 会 argue  这太小了不足以证明 non-paraphrastic chains 有 qualitatively different depth dynamics。\\\"Both chain types  show comparable (and modest) depth signal, suggesting the phenomenon is generic generation drift rather  than the differential depth response the authors claim.\\\" Paraphrastic chains 的 gen-2 vs gen-3 confusion  rate (0.62) 比 continuation (0.51) 更高，但 gen-0 vs gen-1 distinction 在两者中都 robust——说明 depth  signal 本质上是 binary (near-source vs deeper)，不是 true ordinal。Attractor convergence 被确认但  反而成为 negative evidence：\\\"if paraphrasting chains converge within ~3 iterations, and non-paraphrastic  chains show only 3.3 pp more depth signal, the 'novel' non-paraphrastic depth estimation adds negligible  value over studying convergence itself.\\\"\\n\"\n559\t  },\n560\t  {\n561\t    \"name\": \"cross_model_chains\",\n562\t    \"description\": \"Cross-model chains (每个 depth step 使用不同 generator) vs single-model chains。5-gen subset,  generator-level LOGO。\\n\",\n563\t    \"results\": {\n564\t      \"cross_model_binary_f1\": 0.764,\n565\t      \"cross_model_3class_f1\": 0.789,\n566\t      \"single_model_binary_f1\": 0.694,\n567\t      \"single_model_3class_f1\": 0.762,\n568\t      \"cross_model_logo_binary_f1\": 0.83,\n569\t      \"delta_binary_pp\": 7.0,\n570\t      \"delta_logo_pp\": 13.6\n571\t    },\n572\t    \"tables\": [\n573\t      {\n574\t        \"caption\": \"Cross-model vs single-model chain classification\",\n575\t        \"rows\": [\n576\t          [\n577\t            \"Setting\",\n578\t            \"Binary F1\",\n579\t            \"3-class F1\",\n580\t            \"LOGO Binary F1\"\n581\t          ],\n582\t          [\n583\t            \"Single-model chains\",\n584\t            \"0.694\",\n585\t            \"0.762\",\n586\t            \"0.694\"\n587\t          ],\n588\t          [\n589\t            \"Cross-model chains\",\n590\t            \"0.764\",\n591\t            \"0.789\",\n592\t            \"0.830\"\n593\t          ],\n594\t          [\n595\t            \"Δ\",\n596\t            \"+7.0 pp\",\n597\t            \"+2.7 pp\",\n598\t            \"+13.6 pp\"\n599\t          ]\n600\t        ]\n601\t      }\n602\t    ],\n603\t    \"figures\": [],\n604\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model improvement 是 double-edged sword。在 worst 档下，0.830 是 \\\"cheating number\\\" (conflates  depth with generator identity)，0.694 是 \\\"honest number\\\" (single-model, pure depth signal)。Paper 如果 同时 report 两者，reviewer 会 focus on 差距作为方法不是真正测量 depth 的 evidence。如果只 report 0.694， reviewer 会问 \\\"where are the cross-model results?\\\" 无法赢。\\n\\n\\nCross-model chains binary F1 大幅高于 single-model (0.764 vs 0.694, +7 pp; LOGO 0.830 vs 0.694, +13.6 pp)。 Worst-tier reviewer 会 reframe 这为 devastating counter-evidence：\\\"The +13.6 pp LOGO improvement on  cross-model chains reveals that the method is primarily detecting generator switching (different model  fingerprints at each depth step) rather than generation depth. In the single-model case — which is the  harder, more interesting, and more realistic scenario for same-generator iterative contamination — F1 drops  back to the modest 0.694.\\\" Cross-model improvement 被解释为 trivially explained by OOD detection of  different model fingerprints。\\\"The authors' best result (0.830) is achieved on the easiest setting that  conflates depth with generator identity. The honest number for depth classification is 0.694, achieved  on single-model chains where the confound is absent.\\\" 这直接 undercuts the paper's strongest metric。\\n\"\n605\t  },\n606\t  {\n607\t    \"name\": \"multi_domain_seeds\",\n608\t    \"description\": \"扩展到 4 domains: Wikipedia, news (CNN/DailyMail), academic (S2ORC), code。500 seeds × 5 depths per domain。 Cross-domain LOGO evaluation。\\n\",\n609\t    \"results\": {\n610\t      \"wikipedia_binary_f1\": 0.815,\n611\t      \"news_binary_f1\": 0.712,\n612\t      \"news_binary_ci\": [\n613\t        0.69,\n614\t        0.733\n615\t      ],\n616\t      \"academic_binary_f1\": 0.628,\n617\t      \"academic_binary_ci\": [\n618\t        0.603,\n619\t        0.652\n620\t      ],\n621\t      \"code_binary_f1\": 0.687,\n622\t      \"code_binary_ci\": [\n623\t        0.664,\n624\t        0.71\n625\t      ],\n626\t      \"cross_domain_logo_binary_f1\": 0.668,\n627\t      \"max_gap_vs_wiki_pp\": 18.7,\n628\t      \"worst_domain\": \"academic\",\n629\t      \"best_domain\": \"wikipedia\"\n630\t    },\n631\t    \"tables\": [\n632\t      {\n633\t        \"caption\": \"Per-domain binary F1 (LOGO across generators)\",\n634\t        \"rows\": [\n635\t          [\n636\t            \"Domain\",\n637\t            \"Seeds\",\n638\t            \"Binary F1\",\n639\t            \"95% CI\",\n640\t            \"Δ vs Wiki\"\n641\t          ],\n642\t          [\n643\t            \"Wikipedia\",\n644\t            \"500\",\n645\t            \"0.815\",\n646\t            \"[0.796, 0.834]\",\n647\t            \"—\"\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            \"News\",\n651\t            \"500\",\n652\t            \"0.712\",\n653\t            \"[0.690, 0.733]\",\n654\t            \"−10.3 pp\"\n655\t          ],\n656\t          [\n657\t            \"Code\",\n658\t            \"500\",\n659\t            \"0.687\",\n660\t            \"[0.664, 0.710]\",\n661\t            \"−12.8 pp\"\n662\t          ],\n663\t          [\n664\t            \"Academic\",\n665\t            \"500\",\n666\t            \"0.628\",\n667\t            \"[0.603, 0.652]\",\n668\t            \"−18.7 pp\"\n669\t          ],\n670\t          [\n671\t            \"**Cross-domain LOGO**\",\n672\t            \"2000\",\n673\t            \"**0.668**\",\n674\t            \"[0.654, 0.682]\",\n675\t            \"—\"\n676\t          ]\n677\t        ]\n678\t      }\n679\t    ],\n680\t    \"figures\": [],\n681\t    \"analysis\": \"Domain dependence 在 worst 档下与 generator/temperature/instruct/edit 依赖 叠加。Reviewer 列出  cumulative conditions：\\\"base models only, temperature ∈ [0.5, 0.9], continuation preferred,  Wikipedia domain, no human editing, single reference model.\\\" 这是 increasingly narrow niche。 Academic domain failure 尤其 damaging 因为 paper motivation 中引用了 \\\"7–17% of recent scientific  papers contain LLM text\\\"——方法恰好在这个最相关 domain 上最弱。\\n\\n\\nWikipedia (训练数据主 domain) 表现最好 (0.815)，academic 最差 (0.628)——gap 达 18.7 pp。在 t=0.7 下 academic binary F1 进一步降到 ~0.628，接近 chance + 0.128 margin。Cross-domain LOGO (train on 3, test  on 1) 降到 0.668。Worst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"The method's performance is catastrophically  domain-dependent. Scientific text — precisely the domain where AI contamination is a pressing concern  per the authors' own motivation — yields near-chance binary F1 of 0.628. This domain sensitivity,  combined with the base-model and temperature restrictions, makes the method's scope so narrow as to  be practically meaningless.\\\" Academic domain 的 weak signal 可能因为 scientific text 的 formulaic  structure 本身就限制了 vocabulary diversity variation，使 surface features 失效。Cross-domain LOGO  0.668 加上 cross-generator LOGO 0.694 = cumulative degradation when both unknowns (generator + domain)  are combined，reviewer 会 estimate real-world F1 < 0.65。\\n\"\n682\t  },\n683\t  {\n684\t    \"name\": \"finer_grained_ordinal\",\n685\t    \"description\": \"5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4)。测试 depth resolution 是否超过 3-class。 Ordinal methods (CORAL, Frank-Hall) 比较。\\n\",\n686\t    \"results\": {\n687\t      \"five_class_macro_f1\": 0.498,\n688\t      \"five_class_ci\": [\n689\t        0.48,\n690\t        0.516\n691\t      ],\n692\t      \"three_class_macro_f1\": 0.762,\n693\t      \"ordinal_coral_f1\": 0.502,\n694\t      \"ordinal_frank_hall_f1\": 0.491,\n695\t      \"gen0_recall\": 0.92,\n696\t      \"gen1_recall\": 0.63,\n697\t      \"gen2_recall\": 0.41,\n698\t      \"gen3_recall\": 0.33,\n699\t      \"gen4_recall\": 0.29,\n700\t      \"gen2_gen3_confusion_rate\": 0.51,\n701\t      \"gen3_gen4_confusion_rate\": 0.48,\n702\t      \"mean_absolute_depth_error\": 0.89\n703\t    },\n704\t    \"tables\": [\n705\t      {\n706\t        \"caption\": \"Ordinal depth classification resolution\",\n707\t        \"rows\": [\n708\t          [\n709\t            \"Granularity\",\n710\t            \"Method\",\n711\t            \"Macro F1\",\n712\t            \"Ordinal vs XGBoost\"\n713\t          ],\n714\t          [\n715\t            \"3-class\",\n716\t            \"XGBoost\",\n717\t            \"0.762\",\n718\t            \"—\"\n719\t          ],\n720\t          [\n721\t            \"5-class\",\n722\t            \"XGBoost\",\n723\t            \"0.498\",\n724\t            \"—\"\n725\t          ],\n726\t          [\n727\t            \"5-class\",\n728\t            \"CORAL\",\n729\t            \"0.502\",\n730\t            \"+0.4 pp\"\n731\t          ],\n732\t          [\n733\t            \"5-class\",\n734\t            \"Frank-Hall\",\n735\t            \"0.491\",\n736\t            \"−0.7 pp\"\n737\t          ]\n738\t        ]\n739\t      },\n740\t      {\n741\t        \"caption\": \"5-class per-depth recall\",\n742\t        \"rows\": [\n743\t          [\n744\t            \"Depth\",\n745\t            \"Recall\",\n746\t            \"Primary Confusion\"\n747\t          ],\n748\t          [\n749\t            \"gen-0\",\n750\t            \"0.92\",\n751\t            \"gen-1 (6%)\"\n752\t          ],\n753\t          [\n754\t            \"gen-1\",\n755\t            \"0.63\",\n756\t            \"gen-2 (24%)\"\n757\t          ],\n758\t          [\n759\t            \"gen-2\",\n760\t            \"0.41\",\n761\t            \"gen-1/gen-3 (26%/18%)\"\n762\t          ],\n763\t          [\n764\t            \"gen-3\",\n765\t            \"0.33\",\n766\t            \"gen-2/gen-4 (31%/21%)\"\n767\t          ],\n768\t          [\n769\t            \"gen-4\",\n770\t            \"0.29\",\n771\t            \"gen-3 (38%)\"\n772\t          ]\n773\t        ]\n774\t      }\n775\t    ],\n776\t    \"figures\": [],\n777\t    \"analysis\": \"5-class collapse 是 worst 档对 task formulation novelty 最有力的 attack。如果 depth signal 本质上 是 binary (+gen-1 略有区分)，那 \\\"generation depth classification\\\" 这个 task formulation 的 novelty  = 在 binary detection 上加了一个勉强可用的 third class。Ordinal methods 无改善进一步说明 depth  不是 ordinal quantity (continuous gradient)——而是 discrete jump from near-source to deep,  与 model collapse theory 的 gradual degradation 预测不一致。\\n\\n\\n5-class F1 = 0.498 (random baseline ~0.20, so margin = 0.298)。Ordinal methods 无改善 (CORAL 0.502,  Frank-Hall 0.491)——depth signal 不具备 ordinal structure beyond coarse binning。Gen-0 recall 高  (0.92) 但 gen-2/3/4 几乎无法区分 (recall 0.29–0.41, confusion 48–51%)。Gen-0 的高 recall 来自  seed-sharing (原始人类文本与训练 features 有 distributional gap)——这不是 depth classification 而是  human-vs-machine detection。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"5-class F1 of 0.498 confirms depth signal is essentially binary: the  method distinguishes 'source-adjacent' (gen-0/1) from 'deep' (gen-2+) but cannot resolve within either  group. The 3-class formulation is not a principled task definition but an artifact of signal weakness —  it happens to be the granularity at which the method achieves non-trivial performance. The gen-2/3/4  confusion block (48–51% confusion rate) shows the 'generation depth' framing overclaims — this is  at most a binary-plus-one classifier.\\\"\\n\"\n778\t  },\n779\t  {\n780\t    \"name\": \"human_edit_robustness\",\n781\t    \"description\": \"Robustness to simulated human edits: (A) random word replacement 5/10/20%,  (B) LLM-simulated light rephrasing (Qwen3-1.7B)。\\n\",\n782\t    \"results\": {\n783\t      \"baseline_binary_f1\": 0.695,\n784\t      \"random_5pct_f1\": 0.65,\n785\t      \"random_10pct_f1\": 0.614,\n786\t      \"random_20pct_f1\": 0.591,\n787\t      \"llm_rephrase_binary_f1\": 0.647,\n788\t      \"llm_rephrase_multiclass_f1\": 0.667,\n789\t      \"llm_rephrase_edit_distance\": 0.507,\n790\t      \"degradation_5pct_pp\": -4.5,\n791\t      \"degradation_10pct_pp\": -8.1,\n792\t      \"degradation_20pct_pp\": -10.4,\n793\t      \"degradation_llm_pp\": -4.5\n794\t    },\n795\t    \"tables\": [\n796\t      {\n797\t        \"caption\": \"Robustness to simulated human edits\",\n798\t        \"rows\": [\n799\t          [\n800\t            \"Perturbation\",\n801\t            \"Binary F1\",\n802\t            \"Δ vs Baseline\",\n803\t            \"Edit Distance\"\n804\t          ],\n805\t          [\n806\t            \"None (baseline)\",\n807\t            \"0.695\",\n808\t            \"—\",\n809\t            \"0.0\"\n810\t          ],\n811\t          [\n812\t            \"Random 5%\",\n813\t            \"0.650\",\n814\t            \"−4.5 pp\",\n815\t            \"~0.05\"\n816\t          ],\n817\t          [\n818\t            \"Random 10%\",\n819\t            \"0.614\",\n820\t            \"−8.1 pp\",\n821\t            \"~0.10\"\n822\t          ],\n823\t          [\n824\t            \"Random 20%\",\n825\t            \"0.591\",\n826\t            \"−10.4 pp\",\n827\t            \"~0.20\"\n828\t          ],\n829\t          [\n830\t            \"LLM rephrase\",\n831\t            \"0.647\",\n832\t            \"−4.5 pp\",\n833\t            \"0.507\"\n834\t          ]\n835\t        ]\n836\t      }\n837\t    ],\n838\t    \"figures\": [],\n839\t    \"analysis\": \"Robustness 实验在 worst 档下是 lose-lose。Fragile result confirms depth signal 是 surface-level  且 easily disrupted。Combined with instruct degradation、temperature sensitivity、domain dependence， the cumulative fragility makes a devastating picture for any practical deployment argument。\\n\\n\\n5% random replacement 造成 4.5 pp drop (0.695 → 0.650)。LLM rephrasing (edit distance 0.507,  avg 1.69 sentences replaced) 造成相同量级 drop (−4.5 pp → 0.647)。20% replacement 降到 0.591。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"In practice, AI-generated text is almost always edited before  publication — students edit LLM essays, writers revise LLM drafts, automated pipelines post-process  outputs. The method loses 4.5 pp F1 from light editing (50% edit distance ratio, ~1.7 sentences  changed), pushing the already-modest 0.695 baseline to 0.647. At this level, the method correctly  classifies depth for barely 65% of edited text — not actionable for any real-world application.\\\"\\nDegradation is near-linear with perturbation intensity, suggesting the depth signal resides in  surface-level distributional properties easily disrupted by any text modification. This confirms  the \\\"vocabulary impoverishment repackaging\\\" critique—if the signal were capturing deeper structural  properties of recursive generation, it would be more robust to superficial edits.\\n\"\n840\t  },\n841\t  {\n842\t    \"name\": \"ld_score_feature\",\n843\t    \"description\": \"添加 LD-Score (character-distribution signature) 作为第 8 个 feature。测试 character-level 信号 是否与 word/entropy features 互补。\\n\",\n844\t    \"results\": {\n845\t      \"seven_feature_logo_f1\": 0.798,\n846\t      \"eight_feature_with_ld_f1\": 0.802,\n847\t      \"ld_score_alone_logo_f1\": 0.721,\n848\t      \"ld_score_alone_spearman\": 0.794,\n849\t      \"marginal_improvement_pp\": 0.4,\n850\t      \"feature_importance_ld\": 0.022,\n851\t      \"ld_score_cv_corrected_f1\": 0.793\n852\t    },\n853\t    \"tables\": [\n854\t      {\n855\t        \"caption\": \"LD-Score feature addition (3-class LOGO)\",\n856\t        \"rows\": [\n857\t          [\n858\t            \"Feature Set\",\n859\t            \"LOGO F1\",\n860\t            \"Δ\"\n861\t          ],\n862\t          [\n863\t            \"7 features (baseline)\",\n864\t            \"0.798\",\n865\t            \"—\"\n866\t          ],\n867\t          [\n868\t            \"7 + LD-Score\",\n869\t            \"0.802\",\n870\t            \"+0.4 pp\"\n871\t          ],\n872\t          [\n873\t            \"LD-Score only\",\n874\t            \"0.721\",\n875\t            \"—\"\n876\t          ]\n877\t        ]\n878\t      }\n879\t    ],\n880\t    \"figures\": [],\n881\t    \"analysis\": \"Minor experiment, minor result。在 worst 档下主要作为 \\\"all signals converge\\\" narrative 的  supporting evidence。不是 primary attack vector。\\n\\n\\nLD-Score 单独 LOGO F1 = 0.721 (高于 FastDetectGPT 0.627 和 Binoculars 0.579，但低于 Avg-LogProb  0.765 和 7-feature 0.798)。加入后 marginal improvement 仅 0.4 pp (0.798 → 0.802)，feature  importance 排最后 (0.022)。LD-Score 的 high Spearman (0.794) 说明它有 ordinal depth signal， 但被 existing features 高度 subsume。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 不会直接 attack 这个实验 (minor addition)，但会用它 reinforce vocabulary  impoverishment narrative：\\\"Adding a character-level feature provides negligible improvement (0.4 pp),  confirming that character, word, and NLL features all measure the same underlying phenomenon —  text simplification under recursive generation. The claimed 'differential depth response' across  feature types is an artifact of measuring the same signal at different linguistic levels.\\\"\\n\"\n882\t  },\n883\t  {\n884\t    \"name\": \"end_to_end_classifier\",\n885\t    \"description\": \"QLoRA fine-tuned end-to-end depth classifier (OLMo-1B-Instruct, Qwen3-1.7B-Instruct,  及其 base model variants)。Within-distribution CV 和 cross-generator transfer。\\n\",\n886\t    \"results\": {\n887\t      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_3class\": 0.888,\n888\t      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_3class_std\": 0.007,\n889\t      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_binary\": 0.836,\n890\t      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_binary_std\": 0.01,\n891\t      \"qlora_qwen_instruct_3class\": 0.907,\n892\t      \"qlora_qwen_instruct_binary\": 0.867,\n893\t      \"qlora_olmo_base_3class\": 0.859,\n894\t      \"qlora_olmo_base_binary\": 0.793,\n895\t      \"qlora_qwen_base_3class\": 0.904,\n896\t      \"qlora_qwen_base_binary\": 0.86,\n897\t      \"seven_feature_3class\": 0.762,\n898\t      \"seven_feature_binary\": 0.694,\n899\t      \"delta_3class_pp_olmo\": 12.6,\n900\t      \"delta_binary_pp_olmo\": 14.2,\n901\t      \"qlora_5class_f1\": 0.575,\n902\t      \"qlora_inference_cost_ratio\": 47.0\n903\t    },\n904\t    \"tables\": [\n905\t      {\n906\t        \"caption\": \"End-to-end (QLoRA) vs 7-feature ensemble\",\n907\t        \"rows\": [\n908\t          [\n909\t            \"Method\",\n910\t            \"Model\",\n911\t            \"3-class F1 (±std)\",\n912\t            \"Binary F1 (±std)\",\n913\t            \"Cost Ratio\"\n914\t          ],\n915\t          [\n916\t            \"7-feature XGBoost\",\n917\t            \"—\",\n918\t            \"0.762\",\n919\t            \"0.694\",\n920\t            \"1×\"\n921\t          ],\n922\t          [\n923\t            \"QLoRA\",\n924\t            \"OLMo-Instruct\",\n925\t            \"0.888 ± 0.007\",\n926\t            \"0.836 ± 0.010\",\n927\t            \"47×\"\n928\t          ],\n929\t          [\n930\t            \"QLoRA\",\n931\t            \"Qwen-Instruct\",\n932\t            \"0.907 ± 0.008\",\n933\t            \"0.867 ± 0.014\",\n934\t            \"47×\"\n935\t          ],\n936\t          [\n937\t            \"QLoRA\",\n938\t            \"OLMo-Base\",\n939\t            \"0.859 ± 0.004\",\n940\t            \"0.793 ± 0.010\",\n941\t            \"47×\"\n942\t          ],\n943\t          [\n944\t            \"QLoRA\",\n945\t            \"Qwen-Base\",\n946\t            \"0.904 ± 0.009\",\n947\t            \"0.860 ± 0.012\",\n948\t            \"47×\"\n949\t          ]\n950\t        ]\n951\t      }\n952\t    ],\n953\t    \"figures\": [],\n954\t    \"analysis\": \"End-to-end comparison 在 worst 档下 devastating。14-17 pp gap 说明 7-feature ensemble 遗漏了  substantial depth signal。论文的 positioning 是 efficiency vs absolute performance tradeoff，但  worst-tier reviewer 不买账：\\\"if the features miss this much signal, the contribution is not a  competitive method but an incomplete characterization.\\\" QLoRA instruct > base 也 undermine  \\\"instruct kills depth signal\\\" narrative——within-distribution instruct QLoRA actually works fine,  说明 instruct 限制的是 the specific features chosen, not the depth signal itself。\\n\\n\\nQLoRA within-distribution 大幅碾压 7-feature：OLMo-Instruct 3-class 0.888 vs 0.762 (+12.6 pp)， binary 0.836 vs 0.694 (+14.2 pp)。Qwen-Instruct 更高 (3-class 0.907, binary 0.867)。Even base  models QLoRA (3-class 0.859/0.904) 远超 7-feature。5-class F1 = 0.575 也远超 7-feature 的 ~0.50。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 cherry-pick within-distribution numbers：\\\"A straightforward QLoRA classifier  achieves 0.867 binary F1 (Qwen-Instruct), dwarfing the proposed method's 0.694 by 17.3 pp. Even  with the base model alone, QLoRA achieves 0.860 binary — a 16.6 pp advantage. The 7-feature  ensemble captures less than half the depth signal available in the text. The authors' efficiency  argument (47× cost ratio) is unconvincing: the QLoRA classifier runs on the same-sized model  already needed as a reference, and the 17 pp gap is too large to justify on cost grounds.\\\"\\n论文的 rebuttal point 是 LOGO cross-generator transfer——QLoRA within-distribution 的 advantage  partly comes from overfitting to generator-specific patterns。但 worst-tier reviewer 已经 scored  low before considering this nuance。\\n\"\n955\t  },\n956\t  {\n957\t    \"name\": \"text_length_control\",\n958\t    \"description\": \"Address text length confound: (A) length-depth correlation analysis, (B) length-normalized features,  (C) length-matched subsampling re-evaluation。\\n\",\n959\t    \"results\": {\n960\t      \"spearman_length_depth\": 0.12,\n961\t      \"spearman_p\": 0.001,\n962\t      \"length_depth_correlation\": \"weak (|ρ|<0.14)\",\n963\t      \"length_matched_binary_f1\": 0.724,\n964\t      \"unmatched_binary_f1\": 0.77,\n965\t      \"delta_pp\": -4.6,\n966\t      \"normalized_ttr_trend_preserved\": true,\n967\t      \"normalized_hapax_trend_preserved\": true,\n968\t      \"normalized_rho_stronger\": true,\n969\t      \"length_is_primary_confound\": false,\n970\t      \"short_text_dropout_bias\": true,\n971\t      \"length_matched_f1_vs_logo_headline\": \"+3.0 pp above 0.694 LOGO\"\n972\t    },\n973\t    \"tables\": [\n974\t      {\n975\t        \"caption\": \"Length control analysis\",\n976\t        \"rows\": [\n977\t          [\n978\t            \"Condition\",\n979\t            \"Binary F1\",\n980\t            \"Δ vs Unmatched\"\n981\t          ],\n982\t          [\n983\t            \"Unmatched (original)\",\n984\t            \"0.770\",\n985\t            \"—\"\n986\t          ],\n987\t          [\n988\t            \"Length-normalized features\",\n989\t            \"0.748\",\n990\t            \"−2.2 pp\"\n991\t          ],\n992\t          [\n993\t            \"Length-matched subsample\",\n994\t            \"0.724\",\n995\t            \"−4.6 pp\"\n996\t          ]\n997\t        ]\n998\t      }\n999\t    ],\n1000\t    \"figures\": [],\n1001\t    \"analysis\": \"Length confound 不 kill paper 但 erode credibility。4.6 pp 降幅在 worst 档下被 generalize 为  \\\"confound-sensitive method\\\"——reviewer 会 question every reported number 是否被 uncontrolled  confounds inflate。这使 0.694 headline number 的 credibility 进一步下降。\\n\\n\\nLength-depth correlation weak (ρ=0.12) 但 statistically significant (p=0.001)。Length-matched  binary F1 降 4.6 pp (0.770 → 0.724)——意味着 ~6% of signal 来自 text length。Normalized  features 的 depth trend 保持说明 depth signal 不完全是 length artifact，但 worst-tier reviewer  会 magnify 4.6 pp drop：\\\"After controlling for the most basic confound — text length — the method  loses 4.6 pp. How many other confounds (topic, style, vocabulary register) remain uncontrolled?  The 0.694 LOGO F1 may be further inflated by confounds the authors haven't tested.\\\"\\nShort-text dropout bias 增加了 confound complexity：deeper depths 有更多 short text 被 pipeline  过滤掉，导致 surviving deeper text 是 systematically longer/more complete——这是 selection bias， 方法可能部分检测的是 \\\"which texts survived the pipeline filter\\\" 而非 true depth signal。\\n\"\n1002\t  },\n1003\t  {\n1004\t    \"name\": \"large_scale_generator\",\n1005\t    \"description\": \"添加 Qwen3-8B-Base 测试 7B+ scale 的 depth signal。1000 seeds × 5 depths。与现有 6-gen  LOGO 集成。\\n\",\n1006\t    \"results\": {\n1007\t      \"qwen3_8b_records\": 4497,\n1008\t      \"qwen3_8b_unique_seeds\": 995,\n1009\t      \"qwen3_8b_depth_dist\": {\n1010\t        \"0\": 995,\n1011\t        \"1\": 979,\n1012\t        \"2\": 937,\n1013\t        \"3\": 831,\n1014\t        \"4\": 755\n1015\t      },\n1016\t      \"logo_6gen_avg_f1\": 0.789,\n1017\t      \"qwen3_8b_logo_binary_f1\": 0.647,\n1018\t      \"qwen3_8b_logo_3class_f1\": 0.683,\n1019\t      \"qwen3_8b_within_cv_f1\": 0.711,\n1020\t      \"delta_vs_avg_pp\": -10.6,\n1021\t      \"hapax_rho_8b\": -0.558,\n1022\t      \"ttr_rho_8b\": -0.542,\n1023\t      \"entropy_mean_rho_8b\": -0.475,\n1024\t      \"feature_margin_compression_vs_avg\": 0.72,\n1025\t      \"ddr_pattern_preserved\": true\n1026\t    },\n1027\t    \"tables\": [\n1028\t      {\n1029\t        \"caption\": \"Scale effect: Qwen3-8B vs smaller generators\",\n1030\t        \"rows\": [\n1031\t          [\n1032\t            \"Generator\",\n1033\t            \"Size\",\n1034\t            \"LOGO Binary F1\",\n1035\t            \"hapax ρ\",\n1036\t            \"entropy_mean ρ\",\n1037\t            \"Feature compression\"\n1038\t          ],\n1039\t          [\n1040\t            \"Pythia-1B\",\n1041\t            \"1.0B\",\n1042\t            \"0.724\",\n1043\t            \"−0.65\",\n1044\t            \"−0.60\",\n1045\t            \"—\"\n1046\t          ],\n1047\t          [\n1048\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n1049\t            \"1.7B\",\n1050\t            \"0.698\",\n1051\t            \"−0.63\",\n1052\t            \"−0.60\",\n1053\t            \"—\"\n1054\t          ],\n1055\t          [\n1056\t            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n1057\t            \"2.8B\",\n1058\t            \"0.711\",\n1059\t            \"−0.63\",\n1060\t            \"−0.60\",\n1061\t            \"—\"\n1062\t          ],\n1063\t          [\n1064\t            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n1065\t            \"8.0B\",\n1066\t            \"0.647\",\n1067\t            \"−0.56\",\n1068\t            \"−0.48\",\n1069\t            \"0.72×\"\n1070\t          ],\n1071\t          [\n1072\t            \"**Trend**\",\n1073\t            \"—\",\n1074\t            \"**Declining**\",\n1075\t            \"**Compressing**\",\n1076\t            \"**Compressing**\",\n1077\t            \"—\"\n1078\t          ]\n1079\t        ]\n1080\t      }\n1081\t    ],\n1082\t    \"figures\": [],\n1083\t    \"analysis\": \"Scale degradation 是 worst 档的 structural problem。论文诚实 report 这是 scope boundary，但  reviewer reframe：\\\"the scope boundary excludes all models that generate text at scale.\\\" 加上  instruct degradation (OLMo-Instruct LOGO 0.338)，方法的 applicable scope = base models ≤ 8B  at moderate temperature in Wikipedia-like domains without human editing。这个 niche 在 2026 年 没有 practical relevance。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-8B LOGO binary F1 = 0.647——比 6-gen average 低 ~10.6 pp。Feature drift magnitudes 全面压缩  (hapax ρ −0.558 vs avg −0.647, compression ~0.72)。DDR pattern 仍然 preserved (drifting > stationary  分离 maintained)，但 magnitudes 显著 weakened。Within-CV F1 = 0.711 说明 8B 自身 depth signal 存在， 但 cross-generator transfer 弱 (LOGO 0.647)——smaller models 的 feature distribution 不 transfer well。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 extrapolate：\\\"At 8B, the method shows substantial degradation (−10.6 pp vs  average, LOGO binary 0.647). This model is still far from frontier: GPT-4 (>100B), Claude 3 (unknown),  Llama-3-70B — the models generating the vast majority of AI text in practice — are 10–100× larger.  The observed linear degradation in log-scale model size (from 0.6B to 8B) projects to near-chance  performance at frontier scales, rendering the method irrelevant for the contamination problem it claims  to address.\\\" 这是 worst 档中 most damaging extrapolation——审稿人不需要实验数据就可以 argue。\\nDepth distribution (gen-4 only 755/995 = 75.9% retention) 也说明 8B models 更容易产生 degenerate  output at depth (higher skip rate)——selection bias adds to confound concerns。\\n\"\n1084\t  },\n1085\t  {\n1086\t    \"name\": \"ordinal_baseline_comparison\",\n1087\t    \"description\": \"Compare existing detector continuous scores (FastDetectGPT, Binoculars, LD-Score, Avg-LogProb)  作为 ordinal depth predictors vs 7-feature ensemble。Multi-detector ensemble 比较。\\n\",\n1088\t    \"results\": {\n1089\t      \"seven_feature_logo_f1\": 0.798,\n1090\t      \"seven_feature_ci\": [\n1091\t        0.786,\n1092\t        0.799\n1093\t      ],\n1094\t      \"avg_logprob_logo_f1\": 0.765,\n1095\t      \"avg_logprob_ci\": [\n1096\t        0.616,\n1097\t        0.82\n1098\t      ],\n1099\t      \"ld_score_logo_f1\": 0.721,\n1100\t      \"ld_score_ci\": [\n1101\t        0.588,\n1102\t        0.77\n1103\t      ],\n1104\t      \"fastdetectgpt_logo_f1\": 0.627,\n1105\t      \"fastdetectgpt_ci\": [\n1106\t        0.511,\n1107\t        0.762\n1108\t      ],\n1109\t      \"binoculars_logo_f1\": 0.579,\n1110\t      \"binoculars_ci\": [\n1111\t        0.405,\n1112\t        0.664\n1113\t      ],\n1114\t      \"bootstrap_7feat_vs_avglogprob_delta\": 0.033,\n1115\t      \"bootstrap_7feat_vs_avglogprob_p\": 0.0,\n1116\t      \"multi_detector_ensemble_f1\": 0.708,\n1117\t      \"multi_det_4det_plus_surface_3class\": 0.795,\n1118\t      \"multi_det_binary\": 0.708,\n1119\t      \"seven_feature_binary\": 0.705,\n1120\t      \"multi_det_vs_7feat_binary_pp\": 0.3,\n1121\t      \"multi_det_inference_cost\": \"2.4×\"\n1122\t    },\n1123\t    \"tables\": [\n1124\t      {\n1125\t        \"caption\": \"Ordinal depth classification: 7-feature vs existing detector baselines (LOGO)\",\n1126\t        \"rows\": [\n1127\t          [\n1128\t            \"Method\",\n1129\t            \"3-class F1\",\n1130\t            \"95% CI\",\n1131\t            \"Binary F1\",\n1132\t            \"Δ vs 7-feat 3-class\",\n1133\t            \"Bootstrap p\"\n1134\t          ],\n1135\t          [\n1136\t            \"**7-feature ensemble**\",\n1137\t            \"**0.798**\",\n1138\t            \"[0.786, 0.799]\",\n1139\t            \"**0.705**\",\n1140\t            \"—\",\n1141\t            \"—\"\n1142\t          ],\n1143\t          [\n1144\t            \"Avg-LogProb\",\n1145\t            \"0.765\",\n1146\t            \"[0.616, 0.820]\",\n1147\t            \"0.695\",\n1148\t            \"−3.3 pp\",\n1149\t            \"<0.001\"\n1150\t          ],\n1151\t          [\n1152\t            \"LD-Score\",\n1153\t            \"0.721\",\n1154\t            \"[0.588, 0.770]\",\n1155\t            \"0.672\",\n1156\t            \"−7.7 pp\",\n1157\t            \"<0.001\"\n1158\t          ],\n1159\t          [\n1160\t            \"FastDetectGPT\",\n1161\t            \"0.627\",\n1162\t            \"[0.511, 0.762]\",\n1163\t            \"0.601\",\n1164\t            \"−17.1 pp\",\n1165\t            \"<0.001\"\n1166\t          ],\n1167\t          [\n1168\t            \"Binoculars\",\n1169\t            \"0.579\",\n1170\t            \"[0.405, 0.664]\",\n1171\t            \"0.558\",\n1172\t            \"−21.9 pp\",\n1173\t            \"<0.001\"\n1174\t          ],\n1175\t          [\n1176\t            \"4-det + surface\",\n1177\t            \"0.795\",\n1178\t            \"[0.781, 0.808]\",\n1179\t            \"0.708\",\n1180\t            \"−0.3 pp\",\n1181\t            \"0.72\"\n1182\t          ]\n1183\t        ]\n1184\t      }\n1185\t    ],\n1186\t    \"figures\": [],\n1187\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline comparison 在 worst 档下是 most dangerous experiment。在 binary metric (primary) 下， 7-feature (0.705) 和 multi-det (0.708) 几乎无差——reviewer 会 conclude 7-feature 的 contribution  不足以 justify publication。3-class 下 7-feature 略优 (0.798 vs 0.795)，但差距 near-zero。 论文 contribution 被 reduce 为：\\\"a modestly different feature set that performs comparably to  existing detector ensembles, with an interpretive framework (DDR) that may or may not correspond  to a real phenomenon.\\\" 这是 worst 档下 paper's reason to exist 被直接 challenged 的实验。\\n\\n7-feature LOGO F1 = 0.798 (3-class) 显著优于最佳 single detector Avg-LogProb (0.765, δ=3.3 pp,  p < 0.001)。但 single detector CIs 极宽 (Avg-LogProb CI [0.616, 0.820] 跨越 7-feature point  estimate)——说明 per-generator variance 极高。Multi-detector ensemble (4-det + surface) 达到  3-class 0.795 和 binary 0.708 vs 7-feature binary 0.705——仅 0.3 pp 差距。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"The 7-feature ensemble achieves 3.3 pp over Avg-LogProb, but this  single number (average log probability) requires only basic LM inference — no feature engineering,  no reference model selection, no DDR framework. The tiny margin and overlapping confidence intervals  suggest the elaborate DDR characterization provides minimal practical benefit over a trivial baseline.  Moreover, a multi-detector ensemble matches the 7-feature binary F1 within 0.3 pp. The contribution  reduces to: 'a slightly different way to achieve what existing tools already achieve, with a novel  but unvalidated interpretive framework (DDR).'\\\"\\nBootstrap p < 0.001 for 7-feat vs Avg-LogProb 在 3-class setting 是 significant。但 binary  setting 差距 near-zero (0.705 vs 0.708)——primary metric 下 7-feature 反而略低于 multi-detector。\\n\"\n1188\t  }\n1189\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4321cb1-84b0-4cbf-9932-aa6cf3807d7b","uuid":"84ee7a20-2348-4c95-8b8f-53a9ce7fa576","timestamp":"2026-05-21T22:11:59.683Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_3/projects/gen-depth-fingerprint/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T213023/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"feature_ablation_and_trend\",\n    \"description\": \"MVP 数据上三部分分析：(A) Feature ablation: reference-only vs surface-only vs full 7-feature, XGBoost 5-fold CV； (B) 每个 feature 的 depth trend (slope, R², Spearman ρ)；(C) Pythia-410M perplexity pre-validation for Claim 3。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"full_macro_f1\": 0.82,\n      \"surface_only_f1\": 0.763,\n      \"reference_only_f1\": 0.719,\n      \"surface_vs_full_gap_pp\": 5.7,\n      \"ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_ci\": \"[0.706,0.733] vs [0.747,0.774]\",\n      \"mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p\": 0.0,\n      \"mcnemar_full_vs_ref_p\": 0.0,\n      \"h2_features\": \"entropy_mean, ttr, hapax_ratio\",\n      \"h1_features\": \"tail_decay, entropy_std, entropy_max, entropy_min\",\n      \"hapax_ratio_slope\": -0.063,\n      \"hapax_ratio_r2\": 0.88,\n      \"hapax_ratio_rho\": -0.63,\n      \"ttr_slope\": -0.041,\n      \"ttr_r2\": 0.82,\n      \"ttr_rho\": -0.61,\n      \"entropy_mean_slope\": -0.089,\n      \"entropy_mean_r2\": 0.79,\n      \"entropy_mean_rho\": -0.6,\n      \"entropy_std_slope\": -0.031,\n      \"entropy_std_r2\": 0.41,\n      \"entropy_std_rho\": -0.2,\n      \"tail_decay_slope\": 0.003,\n      \"tail_decay_r2\": 0.04,\n      \"tail_decay_rho\": 0.04,\n      \"entropy_max_slope\": 0.008,\n      \"entropy_max_r2\": 0.07,\n      \"entropy_max_rho\": 0.05,\n      \"median_ppl_by_depth\": [\n        13.5,\n        4.96,\n        3.0,\n        2.07,\n        1.72\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Feature ablation: 5-fold CV macro F1 on MVP data (Pythia-2.8B, ~4600 records)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Feature Set\",\n            \"Macro F1\",\n            \"95% CI\",\n            \"Δ vs Full\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full (7 features)\",\n            \"0.820\",\n            \"[0.807, 0.833]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Surface-only (TTR + hapax)\",\n            \"0.763\",\n            \"[0.747, 0.774]\",\n            \"−5.7 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Reference-only (5 entropy)\",\n            \"0.719\",\n            \"[0.706, 0.733]\",\n            \"−10.1 pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Per-feature depth trend (linear regression on depth 0–4)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Feature\",\n            \"Category\",\n            \"Slope\",\n            \"R²\",\n            \"Spearman ρ\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"hapax_ratio\",\n            \"Drifting\",\n            \"−0.063\",\n            \"0.88\",\n            \"−0.63\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TTR\",\n            \"Drifting\",\n            \"−0.041\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"−0.61\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_mean\",\n            \"Drifting\",\n            \"−0.089\",\n            \"0.79\",\n            \"−0.60\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_std\",\n            \"Ambiguous\",\n            \"−0.031\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"−0.20\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_min\",\n            \"Stationary\",\n            \"−0.018\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"−0.15\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"tail_decay\",\n            \"Stationary\",\n            \"+0.003\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"+0.04\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_max\",\n            \"Stationary\",\n            \"+0.008\",\n            \"0.07\",\n            \"+0.05\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在 worst 档下，ablation 的核心问题是 surface features 太强：93% signal retention 意味着 reference features 的  independent contribution minimal。Reviewer 会写：\\\"The proposed DDR framework adds substantial complexity (reference  model inference, 5 entropy features) for a 5.7 pp improvement over two simple vocabulary diversity metrics. The claim  of 'complementary signal' is technically supported but practically marginal.\\\" entropy_std 的 ambiguous status  (R²=0.41, ρ=-0.20) 破坏 DDR clean binary split 的叙事核心，reviewer 会 argue 这是 continuous degradation  而非 bimodal response。\\n\\n\\nSurface-only (0.763) 达到 full (0.820) 的 93%——审稿人会 argue reference features 只是 marginal add-on，不构成独立 contribution。虽然 McNemar p=0 确认显著性，但 worst-tier reviewer 会指出 5.7 pp 差距中 hapax_ratio 单个 surface  feature 就占据了 0.289 importance（plan-002-eval 实测），说明 reference features 被 surface features 的 vocabulary  impoverishment 信号 dominate。entropy_std 的 R²=0.41 处于 drifting/stationary 灰色地带，reviewer 会 argue DDR  不是 bimodal dichotomy 而是 continuous gradient——\\\"the clean split between drifting and stationary is an artifact of  thresholding a continuous degradation spectrum.\\\" 所有 drifting features (hapax, TTR, entropy_mean) 沿同一方向单调递减， reviewer 会 argue 这就是 well-known vocabulary impoverishment 的多种测量维度，不是新现象。Perplexity 单调递减  (13.50→1.72) 只是说明 recursive generation 使 text 对 reference model 更 predictable——这是 trivial observation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_generator_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"扩展到 8 generators (Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B, Llama-3.2-3B, Qwen3-8B,  Mistral-7B-v0.3) 的 LOGO 评估。~37K records。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_records\": 37500,\n      \"generators\": 8,\n      \"families\": 5,\n      \"logo_avg_3class_f1\": 0.762,\n      \"logo_avg_3class_ci\": [\n        0.758,\n        0.766\n      ],\n      \"logo_avg_binary_f1\": 0.694,\n      \"logo_binary_ci\": [\n        0.688,\n        0.7\n      ],\n      \"lofo_binary_f1\": 0.686,\n      \"per_gen_binary_f1\": {\n        \"pythia-1b\": 0.724,\n        \"pythia-2.8b\": 0.711,\n        \"qwen3-0.6b\": 0.702,\n        \"qwen3-1.7b\": 0.698,\n        \"olmo-2-1b\": 0.679,\n        \"llama-3.2-3b\": 0.688,\n        \"qwen3-8b\": 0.647,\n        \"mistral-7b\": 0.633\n      },\n      \"per_gen_range_pp\": 9.1,\n      \"fn_rate_of_binary_errors\": 0.86,\n      \"worst_gen\": \"mistral-7b-v0.3\",\n      \"best_gen\": \"pythia-1b\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Leave-one-generator-out (LOGO) binary F1 (gen-1 vs gen-2+, 8 generators)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Held-out Generator\",\n            \"Family\",\n            \"Size\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"95% CI\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-1B\",\n            \"Pythia\",\n            \"1.0B\",\n            \"0.724\",\n            \"[0.707, 0.741]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n            \"Pythia\",\n            \"2.8B\",\n            \"0.711\",\n            \"[0.693, 0.729]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"0.6B\",\n            \"0.702\",\n            \"[0.682, 0.722]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"1.7B\",\n            \"0.698\",\n            \"[0.678, 0.718]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.2-3B\",\n            \"Llama\",\n            \"3.0B\",\n            \"0.688\",\n            \"[0.668, 0.708]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n            \"OLMo\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"0.679\",\n            \"[0.658, 0.700]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"8.0B\",\n            \"0.647\",\n            \"[0.624, 0.670]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n            \"Mistral\",\n            \"7.0B\",\n            \"0.633\",\n            \"[0.609, 0.657]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**Average**\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"**0.694**\",\n            \"[0.688, 0.700]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Leave-one-family-out (LOFO) binary F1\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Held-out Family\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"Δ vs LOGO\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia\",\n            \"0.668\",\n            \"−2.6 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"0.672\",\n            \"−2.2 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo\",\n            \"0.714\",\n            \"+2.0 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama\",\n            \"0.701\",\n            \"+0.7 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral\",\n            \"0.673\",\n            \"−2.1 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**Average**\",\n            \"**0.686**\",\n            \"**−0.8 pp**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"0.694 是论文 headline number，也是 worst 档审稿人的 primary attack target。两个结构性问题：(1) margin over  chance (0.194) 太薄——在 noisy real-world setting 下可能进一步缩小到 near-chance；(2) per-gen range 9.1 pp  说明 performance 高度 generator-dependent，最差的大模型们恰好是最重要的模型。审稿人会 write：\\\"At the models  that actually generate content at scale (7B+), the method achieves binary F1 of 0.633–0.647, which is  not meaningfully above random guessing for a balanced binary task.\\\"\\n\\n\\nLOGO binary F1 = 0.694，margin over random baseline (0.50) 仅 0.194。在 balanced binary 任务中，这意味着  每 10 个 gen-2+ 样本中约 3 个被误判为 gen-1。Per-gen range 达 9.1 pp (Pythia-1B 0.724 vs Mistral-7B 0.633)， 审稿人会 argue 方法 performance 高度依赖 generator identity，且最差的恰好是两个较大模型 (Mistral-7B 0.633,  Qwen3-8B 0.647)——暗示 scale 上升时方法失效。LOFO binary F1 = 0.686 比 LOGO 低 0.8 pp，说明跨 family 泛化 存在但 margin 更薄。86% 的 binary errors 集中在 FN (gen-2+ 被判为 gen-1)——方法系统性地 under-detect deeper  generation，恰好是实际应用中最需要检出的样本。Reviewer 会写：\\\"The primary metric of 0.694 offers a margin of  less than 0.20 over random guessing. While statistically significant, this margin is far too thin for any  practical deployment, particularly given the 9 pp variance across generators and the systematic FN bias  toward deeper generations.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_family_reference_model\",\n    \"description\": \"测试 OLMo-2-1B 和 Qwen3-0.6B 作为替代 reference model (替代 Pythia-410M)。验证 DDR drift 是否在  非 Pythia reference 下持续存在。Claim 2 的关键 falsification test。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"logo_f1_pythia_ref\": 0.803,\n      \"logo_f1_olmo_ref\": 0.807,\n      \"logo_f1_qwen_ref\": 0.816,\n      \"entropy_mean_drift_pythia_range\": [\n        -1.19,\n        -1.4\n      ],\n      \"entropy_mean_drift_olmo_range\": [\n        -0.61,\n        -0.91\n      ],\n      \"entropy_mean_drift_qwen_range\": [\n        -0.96,\n        -1.35\n      ],\n      \"drift_direction_consistent\": true,\n      \"shape_stationary_all_refs\": true,\n      \"drift_magnitude_ratio_olmo_vs_pythia\": 0.55,\n      \"qwen_ref_gives_best_logo\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Cross-reference-model DDR comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Reference Model\",\n            \"Size\",\n            \"LOGO F1\",\n            \"entropy_mean avg ρ\",\n            \"hapax avg ρ\",\n            \"tail_decay avg ρ\",\n            \"Drift magnitude range\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-410M\",\n            \"410M\",\n            \"0.803\",\n            \"−0.60\",\n            \"−0.63\",\n            \"+0.04\",\n            \"[−1.19, −1.40]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"0.807\",\n            \"−0.50\",\n            \"−0.58\",\n            \"+0.07\",\n            \"[−0.61, −0.91]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n            \"0.6B\",\n            \"0.816\",\n            \"−0.56\",\n            \"−0.61\",\n            \"+0.05\",\n            \"[−0.96, −1.35]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档中最 subtle 的攻击向量。实验技术上通过了 falsification (drift direction consistent, shape  stationary)，但 magnitude dependence on reference model 给了审稿人一个 elegant reframe：\\\"DDR is not a  pure property of recursive generation but a joint function of generation and reference model. The authors'  claim of an 'intrinsic differential response' is overstated—it's a measurement-relative phenomenon.\\\"  这不会导致 reject 但会让 Claim 2 的 contribution 评估降半档。\\n\\n\\nFalsification test 技术上通过了——drift direction 在所有 reference models 下一致 (所有 entropy_mean ρ < 0， 所有 shape features |ρ| < 0.10)。但 drift magnitude 高度依赖 reference model：OLMo reference 的 entropy_mean  drift 仅为 Pythia 的 ~55% (-0.61 vs -1.19 on weakest generator)。LOGO F1 across references 差异小  (0.803–0.816)——但 worst-tier reviewer 会 reframe 这为：\\\"The classification performance is similar regardless  of reference model, but the underlying DDR characterization changes substantially. This means DDR magnitude  is as much a function of reference-generator mismatch as of recursive depth. The phenomenon the authors claim  to study is partially an artifact of their measurement instrument.\\\" 技术上不 kill Claim 2，但 interpretive  precision 被严重削弱。Qwen reference 给出最高 LOGO 说明 reference choice matters——在 worst 档下这被视为  \\\"the method's performance depends on an engineering choice (reference model) that has no principled selection  criterion.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"downstream_utility\",\n    \"description\": \"Fine-tune OLMo-1B on depth-stratified data subsets。3 random seeds, bootstrap CIs。Compare depth-aware  filtering vs binary baselines vs random subsampling。Sample-count-matched comparison。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"all_data_ppl_mean\": 2.335,\n      \"all_data_ppl_std\": 0.0003,\n      \"size_matched_ppl_mean\": 2.367,\n      \"size_matched_ppl_std\": 0.0003,\n      \"depth01_ppl_mean\": 2.387,\n      \"depth01_ppl_std\": 0.0004,\n      \"binary_filtered_ppl_mean\": 2.389,\n      \"binary_filtered_ppl_std\": 0.0006,\n      \"depth0_only_ppl_mean\": 2.681,\n      \"depth0_only_ppl_std\": 0.0006,\n      \"tost_p_2pct\": 0.00011,\n      \"tost_p_1pct\": 0.087,\n      \"ranking\": \"all(2.335) < size_matched(2.367) < depth01(2.387) ≈ binary_filtered(2.389) << depth0_only(2.681)\",\n      \"seed_variance\": \"极小 (<0.002 within variant)\",\n      \"cohens_d_sizematched_vs_depth01\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Downstream CLM perplexity by training data depth composition (3 seeds, OLMo-1B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Variant\",\n            \"Train Size\",\n            \"PPL (mean ± std)\",\n            \"Δ vs Size-matched\",\n            \"TOST ±2% p\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"All depths\",\n            \"12,299\",\n            \"2.335 ± 0.0003\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Size-matched random\",\n            \"3,951\",\n            \"2.367 ± 0.0003\",\n            \"ref\",\n            \"ref\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Depth 0+1 only\",\n            \"3,951\",\n            \"2.387 ± 0.0004\",\n            \"+0.020\",\n            \"1.1×10⁻⁴\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binary filtered\",\n            \"3,951\",\n            \"2.389 ± 0.0006\",\n            \"+0.022\",\n            \"8.7×10⁻⁵\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Depth 0 only\",\n            \"797\",\n            \"2.681 ± 0.0006\",\n            \"+0.314\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Negative finding 是 worst 档的 strategic vulnerability。论文 framing 为 \\\"diagnostic not curative\\\"  是诚实的，但 worst-tier reviewers 会 argue diagnostic value 未被证明——\\\"where is the use case where  knowing depth matters?\\\" 这与 Claim 1 的 practical motivation 形成 circular problem：如果 depth 没有 downstream impact，为什么要分类 depth？论文需要 reframe 为 understanding contribution (DDR characterization)  而非 any form of utility，但这 reframe 在 worst 档下被视为 post-hoc rationalization。\\n\\n\\nNegative finding 极其 clean 且 robust：depth-aware filtering 与 random subsampling 在 ±2% margin 内  equivalence 被 TOST 确认 (p=1.1×10⁻⁴)。Cross-seed variance < 0.002 意味着这个 negative finding 是  highly reliable——不是 noisy null 而是 genuine equivalence。Ranking 显示更多数据 always better (all <  size_matched)，depth filtering 反而 slightly worse than random (2.387 vs 2.367)——意味着 depth-aware  curation 不仅没有帮助，还可能因为丢弃了 useful training signal 而 slightly hurt。\\n审稿人在 worst 档下会 weaponize 这个结果：\\\"The authors' own Claim 3 establishes that generation depth  is informationally vacuous for the most obvious downstream application. If depth information provides  zero utility for data curation — indeed, depth-filtered data is slightly WORSE than random — then the  practical motivation for depth classification collapses entirely. The paper's pivot to 'diagnostic tool'  is an ad hoc rescue, not a designed contribution.\\\" TOST 在 ±1% margin 不显著 (p=0.087) 会被注意到但 不 weaponize (论文已选 ±2%)。depth0_only 的高 perplexity (2.681) 只证明 human vs machine 有区别—— 这是 binary detection 已解决的问题，不支持 depth classification 的 incremental value。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"prompt_type_comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare continuation vs elaboration vs inspired_rewriting chains。1000 seeds × Pythia-2.8B × 3 prompt types。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cv_f1_continuation\": 0.781,\n      \"cv_f1_elaboration\": 0.73,\n      \"cv_f1_rewriting\": 0.737,\n      \"lopto_avg_f1\": 0.753,\n      \"lopto_held_out_cont\": 0.762,\n      \"lopto_held_out_elab\": 0.762,\n      \"lopto_held_out_rewrite\": 0.734,\n      \"depth_retention_cont\": 0.831,\n      \"depth_retention_elab\": 0.986,\n      \"depth_retention_rewrite\": 0.939,\n      \"drift_hapax_cont\": -0.74,\n      \"drift_hapax_elab\": -0.828,\n      \"drift_hapax_rewrite\": -0.8,\n      \"drift_entropy_mean_cont\": -0.557,\n      \"drift_entropy_mean_elab\": -0.471,\n      \"drift_entropy_mean_rewrite\": -0.477,\n      \"spearman_ttr_cont\": -0.629,\n      \"spearman_ttr_elab\": -0.666,\n      \"spearman_ttr_rewrite\": -0.659,\n      \"cross_prompt_type_range_pp\": 5.1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Per-prompt-type classification and drift statistics (Pythia-2.8B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Prompt Type\",\n            \"CV F1\",\n            \"LOPTO F1\",\n            \"Depth Retention\",\n            \"entropy_mean ρ\",\n            \"hapax ρ\",\n            \"TTR ρ\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Continuation\",\n            \"0.781\",\n            \"0.762\",\n            \"0.831\",\n            \"−0.557\",\n            \"−0.740\",\n            \"−0.629\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Elaboration\",\n            \"0.730\",\n            \"0.762\",\n            \"0.986\",\n            \"−0.471\",\n            \"−0.828\",\n            \"−0.666\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Inspired Rewriting\",\n            \"0.737\",\n            \"0.734\",\n            \"0.939\",\n            \"−0.477\",\n            \"−0.800\",\n            \"−0.659\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Prompt-type dependence 在 worst 档下被叠加到 scope limitations 上。Reviewer list: \\\"base models only,  temperature ∈ [0.5, 0.9], continuation chains preferred, Wikipedia seeds.\\\" 每增加一个条件性 qualifier， 方法的 practical scope 进一步收窄。Feature-drift inconsistency (不同 feature 在不同 prompt type 下  rank 不同) 是对 DDR unified framework 的直接挑战。\\n\\n\\nContinuation chains 优于 elaboration 5.1 pp (0.781 vs 0.730)，但 elaboration/rewriting 有更高 depth  retention (0.986/0.939 vs 0.831)。这是一个 paradox：elaboration 保留更多 chain completeness 但 depth  signal 更弱——说明 signal strength 与 chain fidelity inversely correlated。Worst-tier reviewer 会 argue  \\\"the method works best on continuation chains — the simplest, least realistic generation paradigm. In more  naturalistic scenarios (elaboration, rewriting), where generators receive richer prompts and produce more  diverse output, the depth signal degrades by 5 pp.\\\" Feature drift inconsistency across prompt types  (entropy_mean 在 continuation 最强 -0.557 但 hapax 在 elaboration 最强 -0.828) 进一步 undermines DDR  作为 universal phenomenon 的叙事。LOPTO 显示 cross-prompt-type transfer 存在但不完美 (avg 0.753 vs  best within-type 0.781)——在实际应用中 prompt type 未知，reviewer 会 argue 应取 worst-case performance。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"paraphrastic_comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"构建 parallel paraphrasing chains 与 continuation chains 直接比较。测试 attractor convergence theory。 1000 seeds × Pythia-2.8B × 2 chain types。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"paraphrastic_cv_f1\": 0.718,\n      \"continuation_cv_f1\": 0.781,\n      \"paraphrastic_binary_f1\": 0.661,\n      \"continuation_binary_f1\": 0.694,\n      \"paraphrastic_drift_entropy_mean\": -0.39,\n      \"paraphrastic_drift_hapax\": -0.52,\n      \"paraphrastic_depth_retention\": 0.992,\n      \"attractor_convergence_observed\": true,\n      \"effective_classes_paraphrastic\": 2,\n      \"delta_para_vs_cont_binary_pp\": 3.3,\n      \"paraphrastic_gen2_vs_gen3_confusion\": 0.62\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Paraphrastic vs non-paraphrastic chain comparison (Pythia-2.8B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Chain Type\",\n            \"CV F1\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"Depth Retention\",\n            \"entropy_mean ρ\",\n            \"Effective Classes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Continuation (non-para)\",\n            \"0.781\",\n            \"0.694\",\n            \"0.831\",\n            \"−0.557\",\n            \"3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Paraphrastic\",\n            \"0.718\",\n            \"0.661\",\n            \"0.992\",\n            \"−0.390\",\n            \"~2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ\",\n            \"+6.3 pp\",\n            \"+3.3 pp\",\n            \"−0.161\",\n            \"−0.167\",\n            \"+1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Paraphrastic comparison 在 worst 档下 backfires。预期 non-paraphrastic chains 会显示 dramatically  different behavior，但 3.3 pp binary delta 不够 dramatic。反而证明 depth signal 是 generic generation  phenomenon 而非 non-paraphrastic chains 的 unique property。论文需要 reframe 为 \\\"depth signal exists  across chain types with moderate variation\\\" 而非 \\\"non-paraphrastic chains are special\\\"。\\n\\n\\nParaphrastic chains 显示 attractor convergence (depth retention 0.992 ≈ 1.0)，但 depth signal 弱于  non-paraphrastic (binary F1 0.661 vs 0.694, −3.3 pp)。差距只有 3.3 pp——worst-tier reviewer 会 argue  这太小了不足以证明 non-paraphrastic chains 有 qualitatively different depth dynamics。\\\"Both chain types  show comparable (and modest) depth signal, suggesting the phenomenon is generic generation drift rather  than the differential depth response the authors claim.\\\" Paraphrastic chains 的 gen-2 vs gen-3 confusion  rate (0.62) 比 continuation (0.51) 更高，但 gen-0 vs gen-1 distinction 在两者中都 robust——说明 depth  signal 本质上是 binary (near-source vs deeper)，不是 true ordinal。Attractor convergence 被确认但  反而成为 negative evidence：\\\"if paraphrasting chains converge within ~3 iterations, and non-paraphrastic  chains show only 3.3 pp more depth signal, the 'novel' non-paraphrastic depth estimation adds negligible  value over studying convergence itself.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_model_chains\",\n    \"description\": \"Cross-model chains (每个 depth step 使用不同 generator) vs single-model chains。5-gen subset,  generator-level LOGO。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cross_model_binary_f1\": 0.764,\n      \"cross_model_3class_f1\": 0.789,\n      \"single_model_binary_f1\": 0.694,\n      \"single_model_3class_f1\": 0.762,\n      \"cross_model_logo_binary_f1\": 0.83,\n      \"delta_binary_pp\": 7.0,\n      \"delta_logo_pp\": 13.6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Cross-model vs single-model chain classification\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Setting\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"3-class F1\",\n            \"LOGO Binary F1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Single-model chains\",\n            \"0.694\",\n            \"0.762\",\n            \"0.694\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cross-model chains\",\n            \"0.764\",\n            \"0.789\",\n            \"0.830\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ\",\n            \"+7.0 pp\",\n            \"+2.7 pp\",\n            \"+13.6 pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model improvement 是 double-edged sword。在 worst 档下，0.830 是 \\\"cheating number\\\" (conflates  depth with generator identity)，0.694 是 \\\"honest number\\\" (single-model, pure depth signal)。Paper 如果 同时 report 两者，reviewer 会 focus on 差距作为方法不是真正测量 depth 的 evidence。如果只 report 0.694， reviewer 会问 \\\"where are the cross-model results?\\\" 无法赢。\\n\\n\\nCross-model chains binary F1 大幅高于 single-model (0.764 vs 0.694, +7 pp; LOGO 0.830 vs 0.694, +13.6 pp)。 Worst-tier reviewer 会 reframe 这为 devastating counter-evidence：\\\"The +13.6 pp LOGO improvement on  cross-model chains reveals that the method is primarily detecting generator switching (different model  fingerprints at each depth step) rather than generation depth. In the single-model case — which is the  harder, more interesting, and more realistic scenario for same-generator iterative contamination — F1 drops  back to the modest 0.694.\\\" Cross-model improvement 被解释为 trivially explained by OOD detection of  different model fingerprints。\\\"The authors' best result (0.830) is achieved on the easiest setting that  conflates depth with generator identity. The honest number for depth classification is 0.694, achieved  on single-model chains where the confound is absent.\\\" 这直接 undercuts the paper's strongest metric。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_domain_seeds\",\n    \"description\": \"扩展到 4 domains: Wikipedia, news (CNN/DailyMail), academic (S2ORC), code。500 seeds × 5 depths per domain。 Cross-domain LOGO evaluation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wikipedia_binary_f1\": 0.815,\n      \"news_binary_f1\": 0.712,\n      \"news_binary_ci\": [\n        0.69,\n        0.733\n      ],\n      \"academic_binary_f1\": 0.628,\n      \"academic_binary_ci\": [\n        0.603,\n        0.652\n      ],\n      \"code_binary_f1\": 0.687,\n      \"code_binary_ci\": [\n        0.664,\n        0.71\n      ],\n      \"cross_domain_logo_binary_f1\": 0.668,\n      \"max_gap_vs_wiki_pp\": 18.7,\n      \"worst_domain\": \"academic\",\n      \"best_domain\": \"wikipedia\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Per-domain binary F1 (LOGO across generators)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Domain\",\n            \"Seeds\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"95% CI\",\n            \"Δ vs Wiki\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Wikipedia\",\n            \"500\",\n            \"0.815\",\n            \"[0.796, 0.834]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"News\",\n            \"500\",\n            \"0.712\",\n            \"[0.690, 0.733]\",\n            \"−10.3 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Code\",\n            \"500\",\n            \"0.687\",\n            \"[0.664, 0.710]\",\n            \"−12.8 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Academic\",\n            \"500\",\n            \"0.628\",\n            \"[0.603, 0.652]\",\n            \"−18.7 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**Cross-domain LOGO**\",\n            \"2000\",\n            \"**0.668**\",\n            \"[0.654, 0.682]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Domain dependence 在 worst 档下与 generator/temperature/instruct/edit 依赖 叠加。Reviewer 列出  cumulative conditions：\\\"base models only, temperature ∈ [0.5, 0.9], continuation preferred,  Wikipedia domain, no human editing, single reference model.\\\" 这是 increasingly narrow niche。 Academic domain failure 尤其 damaging 因为 paper motivation 中引用了 \\\"7–17% of recent scientific  papers contain LLM text\\\"——方法恰好在这个最相关 domain 上最弱。\\n\\n\\nWikipedia (训练数据主 domain) 表现最好 (0.815)，academic 最差 (0.628)——gap 达 18.7 pp。在 t=0.7 下 academic binary F1 进一步降到 ~0.628，接近 chance + 0.128 margin。Cross-domain LOGO (train on 3, test  on 1) 降到 0.668。Worst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"The method's performance is catastrophically  domain-dependent. Scientific text — precisely the domain where AI contamination is a pressing concern  per the authors' own motivation — yields near-chance binary F1 of 0.628. This domain sensitivity,  combined with the base-model and temperature restrictions, makes the method's scope so narrow as to  be practically meaningless.\\\" Academic domain 的 weak signal 可能因为 scientific text 的 formulaic  structure 本身就限制了 vocabulary diversity variation，使 surface features 失效。Cross-domain LOGO  0.668 加上 cross-generator LOGO 0.694 = cumulative degradation when both unknowns (generator + domain)  are combined，reviewer 会 estimate real-world F1 < 0.65。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"finer_grained_ordinal\",\n    \"description\": \"5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4)。测试 depth resolution 是否超过 3-class。 Ordinal methods (CORAL, Frank-Hall) 比较。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"five_class_macro_f1\": 0.498,\n      \"five_class_ci\": [\n        0.48,\n        0.516\n      ],\n      \"three_class_macro_f1\": 0.762,\n      \"ordinal_coral_f1\": 0.502,\n      \"ordinal_frank_hall_f1\": 0.491,\n      \"gen0_recall\": 0.92,\n      \"gen1_recall\": 0.63,\n      \"gen2_recall\": 0.41,\n      \"gen3_recall\": 0.33,\n      \"gen4_recall\": 0.29,\n      \"gen2_gen3_confusion_rate\": 0.51,\n      \"gen3_gen4_confusion_rate\": 0.48,\n      \"mean_absolute_depth_error\": 0.89\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Ordinal depth classification resolution\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Granularity\",\n            \"Method\",\n            \"Macro F1\",\n            \"Ordinal vs XGBoost\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3-class\",\n            \"XGBoost\",\n            \"0.762\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5-class\",\n            \"XGBoost\",\n            \"0.498\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5-class\",\n            \"CORAL\",\n            \"0.502\",\n            \"+0.4 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5-class\",\n            \"Frank-Hall\",\n            \"0.491\",\n            \"−0.7 pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"5-class per-depth recall\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Depth\",\n            \"Recall\",\n            \"Primary Confusion\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-0\",\n            \"0.92\",\n            \"gen-1 (6%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-1\",\n            \"0.63\",\n            \"gen-2 (24%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-2\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"gen-1/gen-3 (26%/18%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-3\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"gen-2/gen-4 (31%/21%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-4\",\n            \"0.29\",\n            \"gen-3 (38%)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"5-class collapse 是 worst 档对 task formulation novelty 最有力的 attack。如果 depth signal 本质上 是 binary (+gen-1 略有区分)，那 \\\"generation depth classification\\\" 这个 task formulation 的 novelty  = 在 binary detection 上加了一个勉强可用的 third class。Ordinal methods 无改善进一步说明 depth  不是 ordinal quantity (continuous gradient)——而是 discrete jump from near-source to deep,  与 model collapse theory 的 gradual degradation 预测不一致。\\n\\n\\n5-class F1 = 0.498 (random baseline ~0.20, so margin = 0.298)。Ordinal methods 无改善 (CORAL 0.502,  Frank-Hall 0.491)——depth signal 不具备 ordinal structure beyond coarse binning。Gen-0 recall 高  (0.92) 但 gen-2/3/4 几乎无法区分 (recall 0.29–0.41, confusion 48–51%)。Gen-0 的高 recall 来自  seed-sharing (原始人类文本与训练 features 有 distributional gap)——这不是 depth classification 而是  human-vs-machine detection。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"5-class F1 of 0.498 confirms depth signal is essentially binary: the  method distinguishes 'source-adjacent' (gen-0/1) from 'deep' (gen-2+) but cannot resolve within either  group. The 3-class formulation is not a principled task definition but an artifact of signal weakness —  it happens to be the granularity at which the method achieves non-trivial performance. The gen-2/3/4  confusion block (48–51% confusion rate) shows the 'generation depth' framing overclaims — this is  at most a binary-plus-one classifier.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"human_edit_robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"Robustness to simulated human edits: (A) random word replacement 5/10/20%,  (B) LLM-simulated light rephrasing (Qwen3-1.7B)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_binary_f1\": 0.695,\n      \"random_5pct_f1\": 0.65,\n      \"random_10pct_f1\": 0.614,\n      \"random_20pct_f1\": 0.591,\n      \"llm_rephrase_binary_f1\": 0.647,\n      \"llm_rephrase_multiclass_f1\": 0.667,\n      \"llm_rephrase_edit_distance\": 0.507,\n      \"degradation_5pct_pp\": -4.5,\n      \"degradation_10pct_pp\": -8.1,\n      \"degradation_20pct_pp\": -10.4,\n      \"degradation_llm_pp\": -4.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Robustness to simulated human edits\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Perturbation\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"Δ vs Baseline\",\n            \"Edit Distance\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"None (baseline)\",\n            \"0.695\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random 5%\",\n            \"0.650\",\n            \"−4.5 pp\",\n            \"~0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random 10%\",\n            \"0.614\",\n            \"−8.1 pp\",\n            \"~0.10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random 20%\",\n            \"0.591\",\n            \"−10.4 pp\",\n            \"~0.20\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLM rephrase\",\n            \"0.647\",\n            \"−4.5 pp\",\n            \"0.507\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Robustness 实验在 worst 档下是 lose-lose。Fragile result confirms depth signal 是 surface-level  且 easily disrupted。Combined with instruct degradation、temperature sensitivity、domain dependence， the cumulative fragility makes a devastating picture for any practical deployment argument。\\n\\n\\n5% random replacement 造成 4.5 pp drop (0.695 → 0.650)。LLM rephrasing (edit distance 0.507,  avg 1.69 sentences replaced) 造成相同量级 drop (−4.5 pp → 0.647)。20% replacement 降到 0.591。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"In practice, AI-generated text is almost always edited before  publication — students edit LLM essays, writers revise LLM drafts, automated pipelines post-process  outputs. The method loses 4.5 pp F1 from light editing (50% edit distance ratio, ~1.7 sentences  changed), pushing the already-modest 0.695 baseline to 0.647. At this level, the method correctly  classifies depth for barely 65% of edited text — not actionable for any real-world application.\\\"\\nDegradation is near-linear with perturbation intensity, suggesting the depth signal resides in  surface-level distributional properties easily disrupted by any text modification. This confirms  the \\\"vocabulary impoverishment repackaging\\\" critique—if the signal were capturing deeper structural  properties of recursive generation, it would be more robust to superficial edits.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ld_score_feature\",\n    \"description\": \"添加 LD-Score (character-distribution signature) 作为第 8 个 feature。测试 character-level 信号 是否与 word/entropy features 互补。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seven_feature_logo_f1\": 0.798,\n      \"eight_feature_with_ld_f1\": 0.802,\n      \"ld_score_alone_logo_f1\": 0.721,\n      \"ld_score_alone_spearman\": 0.794,\n      \"marginal_improvement_pp\": 0.4,\n      \"feature_importance_ld\": 0.022,\n      \"ld_score_cv_corrected_f1\": 0.793\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"LD-Score feature addition (3-class LOGO)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Feature Set\",\n            \"LOGO F1\",\n            \"Δ\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7 features (baseline)\",\n            \"0.798\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7 + LD-Score\",\n            \"0.802\",\n            \"+0.4 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LD-Score only\",\n            \"0.721\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Minor experiment, minor result。在 worst 档下主要作为 \\\"all signals converge\\\" narrative 的  supporting evidence。不是 primary attack vector。\\n\\n\\nLD-Score 单独 LOGO F1 = 0.721 (高于 FastDetectGPT 0.627 和 Binoculars 0.579，但低于 Avg-LogProb  0.765 和 7-feature 0.798)。加入后 marginal improvement 仅 0.4 pp (0.798 → 0.802)，feature  importance 排最后 (0.022)。LD-Score 的 high Spearman (0.794) 说明它有 ordinal depth signal， 但被 existing features 高度 subsume。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 不会直接 attack 这个实验 (minor addition)，但会用它 reinforce vocabulary  impoverishment narrative：\\\"Adding a character-level feature provides negligible improvement (0.4 pp),  confirming that character, word, and NLL features all measure the same underlying phenomenon —  text simplification under recursive generation. The claimed 'differential depth response' across  feature types is an artifact of measuring the same signal at different linguistic levels.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"end_to_end_classifier\",\n    \"description\": \"QLoRA fine-tuned end-to-end depth classifier (OLMo-1B-Instruct, Qwen3-1.7B-Instruct,  及其 base model variants)。Within-distribution CV 和 cross-generator transfer。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_3class\": 0.888,\n      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_3class_std\": 0.007,\n      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_binary\": 0.836,\n      \"qlora_olmo_instruct_binary_std\": 0.01,\n      \"qlora_qwen_instruct_3class\": 0.907,\n      \"qlora_qwen_instruct_binary\": 0.867,\n      \"qlora_olmo_base_3class\": 0.859,\n      \"qlora_olmo_base_binary\": 0.793,\n      \"qlora_qwen_base_3class\": 0.904,\n      \"qlora_qwen_base_binary\": 0.86,\n      \"seven_feature_3class\": 0.762,\n      \"seven_feature_binary\": 0.694,\n      \"delta_3class_pp_olmo\": 12.6,\n      \"delta_binary_pp_olmo\": 14.2,\n      \"qlora_5class_f1\": 0.575,\n      \"qlora_inference_cost_ratio\": 47.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"End-to-end (QLoRA) vs 7-feature ensemble\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Method\",\n            \"Model\",\n            \"3-class F1 (±std)\",\n            \"Binary F1 (±std)\",\n            \"Cost Ratio\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7-feature XGBoost\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.762\",\n            \"0.694\",\n            \"1×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"QLoRA\",\n            \"OLMo-Instruct\",\n            \"0.888 ± 0.007\",\n            \"0.836 ± 0.010\",\n            \"47×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"QLoRA\",\n            \"Qwen-Instruct\",\n            \"0.907 ± 0.008\",\n            \"0.867 ± 0.014\",\n            \"47×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"QLoRA\",\n            \"OLMo-Base\",\n            \"0.859 ± 0.004\",\n            \"0.793 ± 0.010\",\n            \"47×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"QLoRA\",\n            \"Qwen-Base\",\n            \"0.904 ± 0.009\",\n            \"0.860 ± 0.012\",\n            \"47×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"End-to-end comparison 在 worst 档下 devastating。14-17 pp gap 说明 7-feature ensemble 遗漏了  substantial depth signal。论文的 positioning 是 efficiency vs absolute performance tradeoff，但  worst-tier reviewer 不买账：\\\"if the features miss this much signal, the contribution is not a  competitive method but an incomplete characterization.\\\" QLoRA instruct > base 也 undermine  \\\"instruct kills depth signal\\\" narrative——within-distribution instruct QLoRA actually works fine,  说明 instruct 限制的是 the specific features chosen, not the depth signal itself。\\n\\n\\nQLoRA within-distribution 大幅碾压 7-feature：OLMo-Instruct 3-class 0.888 vs 0.762 (+12.6 pp)， binary 0.836 vs 0.694 (+14.2 pp)。Qwen-Instruct 更高 (3-class 0.907, binary 0.867)。Even base  models QLoRA (3-class 0.859/0.904) 远超 7-feature。5-class F1 = 0.575 也远超 7-feature 的 ~0.50。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 cherry-pick within-distribution numbers：\\\"A straightforward QLoRA classifier  achieves 0.867 binary F1 (Qwen-Instruct), dwarfing the proposed method's 0.694 by 17.3 pp. Even  with the base model alone, QLoRA achieves 0.860 binary — a 16.6 pp advantage. The 7-feature  ensemble captures less than half the depth signal available in the text. The authors' efficiency  argument (47× cost ratio) is unconvincing: the QLoRA classifier runs on the same-sized model  already needed as a reference, and the 17 pp gap is too large to justify on cost grounds.\\\"\\n论文的 rebuttal point 是 LOGO cross-generator transfer——QLoRA within-distribution 的 advantage  partly comes from overfitting to generator-specific patterns。但 worst-tier reviewer 已经 scored  low before considering this nuance。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"text_length_control\",\n    \"description\": \"Address text length confound: (A) length-depth correlation analysis, (B) length-normalized features,  (C) length-matched subsampling re-evaluation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"spearman_length_depth\": 0.12,\n      \"spearman_p\": 0.001,\n      \"length_depth_correlation\": \"weak (|ρ|<0.14)\",\n      \"length_matched_binary_f1\": 0.724,\n      \"unmatched_binary_f1\": 0.77,\n      \"delta_pp\": -4.6,\n      \"normalized_ttr_trend_preserved\": true,\n      \"normalized_hapax_trend_preserved\": true,\n      \"normalized_rho_stronger\": true,\n      \"length_is_primary_confound\": false,\n      \"short_text_dropout_bias\": true,\n      \"length_matched_f1_vs_logo_headline\": \"+3.0 pp above 0.694 LOGO\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Length control analysis\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Condition\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"Δ vs Unmatched\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Unmatched (original)\",\n            \"0.770\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Length-normalized features\",\n            \"0.748\",\n            \"−2.2 pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Length-matched subsample\",\n            \"0.724\",\n            \"−4.6 pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Length confound 不 kill paper 但 erode credibility。4.6 pp 降幅在 worst 档下被 generalize 为  \\\"confound-sensitive method\\\"——reviewer 会 question every reported number 是否被 uncontrolled  confounds inflate。这使 0.694 headline number 的 credibility 进一步下降。\\n\\n\\nLength-depth correlation weak (ρ=0.12) 但 statistically significant (p=0.001)。Length-matched  binary F1 降 4.6 pp (0.770 → 0.724)——意味着 ~6% of signal 来自 text length。Normalized  features 的 depth trend 保持说明 depth signal 不完全是 length artifact，但 worst-tier reviewer  会 magnify 4.6 pp drop：\\\"After controlling for the most basic confound — text length — the method  loses 4.6 pp. How many other confounds (topic, style, vocabulary register) remain uncontrolled?  The 0.694 LOGO F1 may be further inflated by confounds the authors haven't tested.\\\"\\nShort-text dropout bias 增加了 confound complexity：deeper depths 有更多 short text 被 pipeline  过滤掉，导致 surviving deeper text 是 systematically longer/more complete——这是 selection bias， 方法可能部分检测的是 \\\"which texts survived the pipeline filter\\\" 而非 true depth signal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"large_scale_generator\",\n    \"description\": \"添加 Qwen3-8B-Base 测试 7B+ scale 的 depth signal。1000 seeds × 5 depths。与现有 6-gen  LOGO 集成。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen3_8b_records\": 4497,\n      \"qwen3_8b_unique_seeds\": 995,\n      \"qwen3_8b_depth_dist\": {\n        \"0\": 995,\n        \"1\": 979,\n        \"2\": 937,\n        \"3\": 831,\n        \"4\": 755\n      },\n      \"logo_6gen_avg_f1\": 0.789,\n      \"qwen3_8b_logo_binary_f1\": 0.647,\n      \"qwen3_8b_logo_3class_f1\": 0.683,\n      \"qwen3_8b_within_cv_f1\": 0.711,\n      \"delta_vs_avg_pp\": -10.6,\n      \"hapax_rho_8b\": -0.558,\n      \"ttr_rho_8b\": -0.542,\n      \"entropy_mean_rho_8b\": -0.475,\n      \"feature_margin_compression_vs_avg\": 0.72,\n      \"ddr_pattern_preserved\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Scale effect: Qwen3-8B vs smaller generators\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Generator\",\n            \"Size\",\n            \"LOGO Binary F1\",\n            \"hapax ρ\",\n            \"entropy_mean ρ\",\n            \"Feature compression\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-1B\",\n            \"1.0B\",\n            \"0.724\",\n            \"−0.65\",\n            \"−0.60\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            \"1.7B\",\n            \"0.698\",\n            \"−0.63\",\n            \"−0.60\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n            \"2.8B\",\n            \"0.711\",\n            \"−0.63\",\n            \"−0.60\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            \"8.0B\",\n            \"0.647\",\n            \"−0.56\",\n            \"−0.48\",\n            \"0.72×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**Trend**\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"**Declining**\",\n            \"**Compressing**\",\n            \"**Compressing**\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Scale degradation 是 worst 档的 structural problem。论文诚实 report 这是 scope boundary，但  reviewer reframe：\\\"the scope boundary excludes all models that generate text at scale.\\\" 加上  instruct degradation (OLMo-Instruct LOGO 0.338)，方法的 applicable scope = base models ≤ 8B  at moderate temperature in Wikipedia-like domains without human editing。这个 niche 在 2026 年 没有 practical relevance。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-8B LOGO binary F1 = 0.647——比 6-gen average 低 ~10.6 pp。Feature drift magnitudes 全面压缩  (hapax ρ −0.558 vs avg −0.647, compression ~0.72)。DDR pattern 仍然 preserved (drifting > stationary  分离 maintained)，但 magnitudes 显著 weakened。Within-CV F1 = 0.711 说明 8B 自身 depth signal 存在， 但 cross-generator transfer 弱 (LOGO 0.647)——smaller models 的 feature distribution 不 transfer well。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 extrapolate：\\\"At 8B, the method shows substantial degradation (−10.6 pp vs  average, LOGO binary 0.647). This model is still far from frontier: GPT-4 (>100B), Claude 3 (unknown),  Llama-3-70B — the models generating the vast majority of AI text in practice — are 10–100× larger.  The observed linear degradation in log-scale model size (from 0.6B to 8B) projects to near-chance  performance at frontier scales, rendering the method irrelevant for the contamination problem it claims  to address.\\\" 这是 worst 档中 most damaging extrapolation——审稿人不需要实验数据就可以 argue。\\nDepth distribution (gen-4 only 755/995 = 75.9% retention) 也说明 8B models 更容易产生 degenerate  output at depth (higher skip rate)——selection bias adds to confound concerns。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ordinal_baseline_comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare existing detector continuous scores (FastDetectGPT, Binoculars, LD-Score, Avg-LogProb)  作为 ordinal depth predictors vs 7-feature ensemble。Multi-detector ensemble 比较。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seven_feature_logo_f1\": 0.798,\n      \"seven_feature_ci\": [\n        0.786,\n        0.799\n      ],\n      \"avg_logprob_logo_f1\": 0.765,\n      \"avg_logprob_ci\": [\n        0.616,\n        0.82\n      ],\n      \"ld_score_logo_f1\": 0.721,\n      \"ld_score_ci\": [\n        0.588,\n        0.77\n      ],\n      \"fastdetectgpt_logo_f1\": 0.627,\n      \"fastdetectgpt_ci\": [\n        0.511,\n        0.762\n      ],\n      \"binoculars_logo_f1\": 0.579,\n      \"binoculars_ci\": [\n        0.405,\n        0.664\n      ],\n      \"bootstrap_7feat_vs_avglogprob_delta\": 0.033,\n      \"bootstrap_7feat_vs_avglogprob_p\": 0.0,\n      \"multi_detector_ensemble_f1\": 0.708,\n      \"multi_det_4det_plus_surface_3class\": 0.795,\n      \"multi_det_binary\": 0.708,\n      \"seven_feature_binary\": 0.705,\n      \"multi_det_vs_7feat_binary_pp\": 0.3,\n      \"multi_det_inference_cost\": \"2.4×\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Ordinal depth classification: 7-feature vs existing detector baselines (LOGO)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Method\",\n            \"3-class F1\",\n            \"95% CI\",\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"Δ vs 7-feat 3-class\",\n            \"Bootstrap p\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**7-feature ensemble**\",\n            \"**0.798**\",\n            \"[0.786, 0.799]\",\n            \"**0.705**\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Avg-LogProb\",\n            \"0.765\",\n            \"[0.616, 0.820]\",\n            \"0.695\",\n            \"−3.3 pp\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LD-Score\",\n            \"0.721\",\n            \"[0.588, 0.770]\",\n            \"0.672\",\n            \"−7.7 pp\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FastDetectGPT\",\n            \"0.627\",\n            \"[0.511, 0.762]\",\n            \"0.601\",\n            \"−17.1 pp\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binoculars\",\n            \"0.579\",\n            \"[0.405, 0.664]\",\n            \"0.558\",\n            \"−21.9 pp\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4-det + surface\",\n            \"0.795\",\n            \"[0.781, 0.808]\",\n            \"0.708\",\n            \"−0.3 pp\",\n            \"0.72\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline comparison 在 worst 档下是 most dangerous experiment。在 binary metric (primary) 下， 7-feature (0.705) 和 multi-det (0.708) 几乎无差——reviewer 会 conclude 7-feature 的 contribution  不足以 justify publication。3-class 下 7-feature 略优 (0.798 vs 0.795)，但差距 near-zero。 论文 contribution 被 reduce 为：\\\"a modestly different feature set that performs comparably to  existing detector ensembles, with an interpretive framework (DDR) that may or may not correspond  to a real phenomenon.\\\" 这是 worst 档下 paper's reason to exist 被直接 challenged 的实验。\\n\\n7-feature LOGO F1 = 0.798 (3-class) 显著优于最佳 single detector Avg-LogProb (0.765, δ=3.3 pp,  p < 0.001)。但 single detector CIs 极宽 (Avg-LogProb CI [0.616, 0.820] 跨越 7-feature point  estimate)——说明 per-generator variance 极高。Multi-detector ensemble (4-det + surface) 达到  3-class 0.795 和 binary 0.708 vs 7-feature binary 0.705——仅 0.3 pp 差距。\\nWorst-tier reviewer 会 argue：\\\"The 7-feature ensemble achieves 3.3 pp over Avg-LogProb, but this  single number (average log probability) requires only basic LM inference — no feature engineering,  no reference model selection, no DDR framework. The tiny margin and overlapping confidence intervals  suggest the elaborate DDR characterization provides minimal practical benefit over a trivial baseline.  Moreover, a multi-detector ensemble matches the 7-feature binary F1 within 0.3 pp. The contribution  reduces to: 'a slightly different way to achieve what existing tools already achieve, with a novel  but unvalidated interpretive framework (DDR).'\\\"\\nBootstrap p < 0.001 for 7-feat vs Avg-LogProb 在 3-class setting 是 significant。但 binary  setting 差距 near-zero (0.705 vs 0.708)——primary metric 下 7-feature 反而略低于 multi-detector。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1189,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1189}}}
